// Kamerton app (naryad Н1-06): the Telegram long-polling cycle in ONE
// serve program — deploy contract of kamerton.service
// (ExecStart: mlog serve /data/kamerton/app.mlog). The naryad fixes the
// shape: "два cron-тика в одном .mlog" — the morning tick proposes an
// arm (consumes the Н1-05 bandit core mirrored below) and asks for a
// prediction, the evening tick drains getUpdates, writes the answers
// into trial/response and closes unanswered trials as misses at 02:00
// local.
//
// ── Design decisions fixed here (in-boundary choices; the naryad fixes
//    the requirements, not the parametrisation) ─────────────────────────
//   1. Registration: the serve process runs NO top-level statements and
//     NO on_session_start hook at boot (the serve probe: hook file
//     absent, jobs=0). Cron jobs are registered IDEMPOTENTLY from the
//     /setup route (cron_list guard -> cron_add only when missing) and
//     carried across restarts by `memory { persist }` — the jobs and
//     the getUpdates offset survive the service restart (the
//     acceptance row; verified by the serve probes in the worklog).
//   2. Timezone: cron_add matches windows in the job's tz (default
//     MLOG_CRON_TZ else UTC), the deploy allowlist opens
//     KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET (hours, float; MSK=3). The tick expressions
//     are computed FROM the offset with the local wall-clock minutes
//     folded to UTC (no modulo operator — to_int truncation, the
//     bandit explore-idx precedent): 07:00 local under MSK registers
//     as "0 4 * * *", 02:00 local as "0 23 * * *".
//   3. Chat protocol (minimal, wave 1): the morning message proposes
//     the arm and asks for a prediction; the owner answers "p:<0..1>"
//     (prediction depth), "m:<0..1>" (the moment response), anything
//     else is appended to trial.free_note. Every outgoing text passes
//     escape_html — the DB output never reaches the chat raw.
//   4. Exactly-once posture: the Telegram offset (kv tg_offset) is
//     advanced AFTER a batch is processed; a crash before the advance
//     replays the batch and the DB guards make the replay idempotent —
//     the moment insert is guarded by (trial_id, kind), the prediction
//     UPDATE fills an untouched default only, misses are status flips.
//     A repeated free-note append is the one accepted dup window and
//     is declared loudly here.
//   5. Network posture: every http_get carries the per-call deadline
//     (№592) inside 1..=300; the outcome taxonomy is consumed through
//     the sanitize-then-decide form — escape_html (Sanitized =
//     public/trusted) decides the control flow, never the raw label.
//     send_message reads TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from the process env
//     itself and degrades to the [AUDIT] stub without it (probe-pinned),
//     so tests never touch the network.
//   6. Trust boundaries: fetch_updates returns UNTRUSTED network data;
//     the whole update-processing chain runs inside ONE annotated
//     boundary pattern (the parity-tick-route fire_job precedent) —
//     inside it the data is sanctioned and the DB guards decide;
//     outside it the return is never echoed or branched on. The chat
//     filter compares SANITIZED projections.
//   7. Composition: no cross-file imports exist in the language, so
//     this file carries byte-identical mirrors of the store schema
//     (the bandit.mlog precedent), the bandit decision core, the arms
//     seed (§arms-seed) and the mini-app core (§miniapp-core). The
//     canonical copies live in src/bandit/bandit.mlog,
//     src/arms/arms.mlog, src/miniapp/miniapp.mlog and
//     src/telegram/telegram.mlog; the mirror modules carry the
//     APP-MIRROR markers and the block equality is verified by the
//     verifier script recorded in the naryad worklog (read_file
//     refuses *.mlog paths — the №455-sensitive list — so the pin
//     lives outside the language).
//
// Language-discipline notes (§2, declared loudly where relevant):
//   - RESPOND_SWALLOWED (v0.28.2, security Y-1): every respond() is
//     written `return respond(...)` — the fail-closed startup refusal
//     of bare tail responds is the contract on both backends.
//   - env() in route bodies and cron-tick bodies is gated by №259;
//     every name read here (KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN, KAMERTON_CHAT_ID,
//     KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET) is opened by deploy/env.allowlist through
//     METALOGOS_ENV_ALLOWLIST (install.sh derives the runtime value).
//     TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is read INSIDE the send_message builtin
//     (process env) — deliberately NOT in the allowlist.
//   - The D2 loop defect (№598, unfixed in v0.28.2): every sink call
//     inside a loop body uses the assignment shape `let _ = f(...)`; a
//     bare call inside a mixed loop body corrupts the pattern return.
//   - NEW D2-family symptom isolated during this naryad (probe in the
//     worklog): a `while i < len(xs)` loop whose body can reach
//     cron_remove() MISCONVERGES — after the first removal the pass
//     silently drops the remaining iterations (and stdout prints after
//     the first remove are lost), so repeat runs diverge (0 or 2 jobs
//     instead of 1). Every cron-store pass here therefore runs as
//     `each` over the cron_list() snapshot; the symptom is declared to
//     the Metalogos- agent (v0.28.3 task file). The same family, third
//     case: a print() INSIDE an if-body that follows an effect call
//     (cron_remove) inside an each-body silently kills the SUBSEQUENT
//     if/add phase — the registration prints therefore happen ONCE as a
//     post-loop summary, never inside the loop bodies (probe: variant
//     A misconverges, variant B converges). Fourth case, cron-tick
//     lane: a bare `return` inside a nested if-body of a Unit tick
//     pattern dispatches as [UNDEFINED_VARIABLE] "undefined variable:
//     return" — the early-return guards therefore invert into
//     positive-branch blocks (no return under a nested if).
//   - No modulo operator (grammar v0.28.2); to_int truncation
//     arithmetic everywhere a remainder is needed.

// The deploy contract of Н1-02: KAMERTON_DB carries the plain database
// path; the VM lane resolves it lazily at the first db access (№758).
// This file carries NO test blocks: v0.28.2 has no single db-url form
// valid for both lanes (the interpreter test lane needs an entity-ref
// url for the schema replay; the serve boot pass refuses entity refs —
// the §2 declaration below), so the app's tests live in
// src/telegram/telegram.mlog against a literal in-memory db and the
// byte-identical mirror blocks; app.mlog stays the serve canon.
db { url: env("KAMERTON_DB") }

// The KV store carries the getUpdates offset AND the cron job store;
// without persist both die with the process (the serve probe logs).
memory { persist: "data/kamerton-kv.db" }

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: db-cycle (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §db-cycle) ──────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: db-cycle (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §db-cycle) ──────────────────────────────

// ── The schema: the operator-mirror DDL path (§2 declaration) ─────────
// Затык §2 (v0.28.2, заявлен громко в PR/worklog): ONE db-url form for
// BOTH lanes does not exist — `mlog test` (interpreter) requires an
// entity-ref url for the schema replay at declaration time, while the
// serve boot pass refuses entity refs ([UNDEFINED_VARIABLE]) and only
// accepts inline env()/env_or()/literal (№758 lazy). The proposed and
// implemented exit: the schema-as-code block is replaced by the
// ADDITIVE-ONLY idempotent DDL literals of the operator mirror
// (migrations/0001_init.sql, ADR-0183) executed by ensure_schema() —
// called by both ticks and /setup before any query. Byte-equality of
// the DDL to the migration is pinned by the verifier script in the
// worklog.
pattern ensure_schema() -> Unit {
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS arm (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT, group_name TEXT, day_window TEXT, duration_min INTEGER DEFAULT '10', prior_mean REAL DEFAULT '0.0', prior_std REAL DEFAULT '1.0', active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS note (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, body TEXT, active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS trial (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_date TEXT, day_window TEXT, arm_id INTEGER REFERENCES arm(id), note_id INTEGER REFERENCES note(id), status TEXT DEFAULT 'proposed', prediction_depth REAL DEFAULT '0.0', prediction_confidence REAL DEFAULT '0.0', moment_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', moment_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', moment_source TEXT DEFAULT '', next_day_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', next_day_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', action_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', action_present INTEGER DEFAULT '0', reward REAL DEFAULT '0.0', free_note TEXT DEFAULT '', closed_at TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS response (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_id INTEGER REFERENCES trial(id), kind TEXT, depth REAL DEFAULT '0.0', details TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS context (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, trial_id INTEGER REFERENCES trial(id), moon_phase TEXT DEFAULT '', weather TEXT DEFAULT '', sound_mode TEXT DEFAULT '', sleep_quality REAL DEFAULT '0.0', logged_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS candidate (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT, kind TEXT DEFAULT 'non_periodic', status TEXT DEFAULT 'candidate', stat_value REAL DEFAULT '0.0', threshold REAL DEFAULT '0.0', tested_at TEXT DEFAULT '', note TEXT DEFAULT '')", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS practice_session (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, kind TEXT DEFAULT 'pacer', arm_id INTEGER REFERENCES arm(id), trial_id INTEGER REFERENCES trial(id), tempo_bpm REAL DEFAULT '0.0', steps_total INTEGER DEFAULT '0', steps_done INTEGER DEFAULT '0', step_marks TEXT DEFAULT '', rr_json TEXT DEFAULT '', rr_source TEXT DEFAULT '', session_date TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sweep_result (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, session_id INTEGER REFERENCES practice_session(id), result_date TEXT DEFAULT '', resonance_bpm REAL DEFAULT '0.0', peak_freq_bpm REAL DEFAULT '0.0', power_fraction REAL DEFAULT '0.0', p_value REAL DEFAULT '1.0', steps_valid INTEGER DEFAULT '0', steps_total INTEGER DEFAULT '0', prev_resonance_bpm REAL DEFAULT '0.0', freq_delta_bpm REAL DEFAULT '0.0', share_ratio REAL DEFAULT '0.0', verdict TEXT DEFAULT '', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  let _ = db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS practice_text (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, group_name TEXT, body TEXT, active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))", [])
  ensure_indexes()
}

pattern ensure_indexes() -> Unit {
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_date ON trial(trial_date)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_arm ON trial(arm_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_trial_status ON trial(status)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_response_trial ON response(trial_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_context_trial ON context(trial_id)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_candidate_name ON candidate(name)")
  db_execute("CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_arm_active ON arm(active)")
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: store-core (the signatures mirror
//    src/store/store.mlog; equality pinned by the worklog script) ──────

pattern trial_by_id(trial_id: Float) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id, trial_date, day_window, arm_id, status, prediction_depth, prediction_confidence, moment_value, moment_present, moment_source, next_day_value, next_day_present, action_value, action_present, reward FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [trial_id])
}

pattern compute_reward(trial_id: Float) -> Float {
  let rows = query("SELECT moment_value, moment_present, next_day_value, next_day_present, action_value, action_present FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [trial_id])
  if len(rows) == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let r = rows[0]
  let mut acc = 0.0
  let mut wsum = 0.0
  if r.moment_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.2 * r.moment_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.2
  }
  if r.next_day_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.3 * r.next_day_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.3
  }
  if r.action_present == 1.0 {
    acc = acc + 0.5 * r.action_value
    wsum = wsum + 0.5
  }
  if wsum == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let reward = acc / wsum
  db_execute("UPDATE trial SET reward = ? WHERE id = ?", [reward, trial_id])
  return reward
}

// ── Sweep protocol (Н2-06): the individual resonance frequency ──────────
// The tempo sweep (4.5–7.0 breaths/min, two minutes per tempo — the
// Н2-04 pacer protocol) walks the protocol while the Н2-05 PPG records
// the pulse on the device; every completed step carries its RR segment
// in the session's step_marks ({"step","tempo_bpm","rr","rr_reason"}).
// The spectrum of each segment is computed by the language's spectral
// contour (№591 builtins lomb_scargle/spectral_peak): sin/cos are
// absent from the 0.30.0 grammar (probe-pinned), so hand-rolling the
// periodogram is impossible — the builtins are the only honest path.
// The resonance frequency is the PACED tempo of the valid step with
// the maximal power fraction. The preregistration (fixed in the
// naryad BEFORE any live data, docs/volna-2-issues.md Н2-06):
//   - a step counts as valid when its mark carries a non-empty rr
//     array whose spectrum is not degraded (the language's own floor
//     is 12 points — probe-pinned Degraded reason);
//   - the protocol is accepted at >= 6 valid steps of the 11;
//   - the repeat protocol reproduces when the resonance tempo stays
//     within 0.3 breaths/min of the previous recorded run and the
//     winner's power fraction stays within the ratio [0.5; 2.0].
// An accepted run is fixed in the sweep_result table (invariant 6: a
// third-party sqlite3 client reads it) AND mirrored into the persisted
// kv (resonance_* keys, data/kamerton-kv.db) for the live process.

pattern sweep_rr_times(rr_ms: List) -> List {
  // Beat arrival times in seconds: the cumulative sums of the RR
  // intervals. The segment carries no timestamps — the intervals are
  // the full information the page sends (invariant 7 data minimum).
  let mut ts = []
  let mut t = 0.0
  each v in rr_ms {
    t = t + to_float(v) / 1000.0
    ts = push(ts, t)
  }
  return ts
}

pattern sweep_step_peak(rr_ms: List) -> Struct {
  // One step's RR segment -> the spectral verdict. Times are the
  // cumulative arrival seconds, values are the RR intervals in ms.
  // Degraded spectra refuse loudly with a reason — never silently.
  if len(rr_ms) < 12.0 {
    return {ok: false, freq_bpm: 0.0, share: 0.0, p_value: 1.0, reason: "RR-ряд короче 12 точек: " + to_string(len(rr_ms))}
  }
  let ts = sweep_rr_times(rr_ms)
  let spec = lomb_scargle(ts, rr_ms)
  let pk = spectral_peak(spec)
  if pk.degraded == true {
    return {ok: false, freq_bpm: 0.0, share: 0.0, p_value: 1.0, reason: "спектр деградировал: точек " + to_string(len(rr_ms))}
  }
  return {ok: true, freq_bpm: pk.freq * 60.0, share: pk.power_fraction, p_value: pk.p_value, reason: ""}
}

pattern sweep_analyze(marks_json: String<public, trusted>) -> Struct {
  // The session's step_marks (the page-written JSON array) -> the sweep
  // verdict. Loud refusals: not a JSON array, zero valid steps, fewer
  // than the preregistered 6 valid steps. Marks predating the Н2-06
  // shape (no rr key — an old-format writer or the toggle off) count as
  // invalid steps; the field probe rides json_encode + contains because
  // a missing struct field fails LOUDLY on 0.30.0 (probe-pinned) and
  // the analyzer must classify, not crash.
  let parsed = parse_json(marks_json)
  if type_of(parsed) != "List" {
    return {ok: false, reason: "step_marks: ожидается JSON-массив отметок шагов", resonance_bpm: 0.0, peak_freq_bpm: 0.0, share: 0.0, p_value: 1.0, steps_valid: 0.0, steps_total: 0.0}
  }
  let mut total = 0.0
  let mut valid = 0.0
  let mut best_bpm = 0.0
  let mut best_freq = 0.0
  let mut best_share = 0.0
  let mut best_p = 1.0
  each m in parsed {
    total = total + 1.0
    let mj = json_encode(m)
    if contains(mj, "\"rr\"") == false {
      let _ = mj
    } else {
      if contains(mj, "\"tempo_bpm\"") == false {
        let _ = mj
      } else {
        if type_of(m.rr) == "List" {
          if len(m.rr) > 0.0 {
            let pk = sweep_step_peak(m.rr)
            if pk.ok == true {
              valid = valid + 1.0
              if pk.share > best_share {
                best_share = pk.share
                best_bpm = to_float(m.tempo_bpm)
                best_freq = pk.freq_bpm
                best_p = pk.p_value
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  if valid == 0.0 {
    return {ok: false, reason: "годных RR-сегментов нет: 0 из " + to_string(total), resonance_bpm: 0.0, peak_freq_bpm: 0.0, share: 0.0, p_value: 1.0, steps_valid: 0.0, steps_total: total}
  }
  if valid < 6.0 {
    return {ok: false, reason: "шагов с годным спектром: " + to_string(valid) + " из " + to_string(total) + " — протокол требует не менее 6 (предрегистрация Н2-06)", resonance_bpm: 0.0, peak_freq_bpm: 0.0, share: 0.0, p_value: 1.0, steps_valid: valid, steps_total: total}
  }
  return {ok: true, reason: "", resonance_bpm: best_bpm, peak_freq_bpm: best_freq, share: best_share, p_value: best_p, steps_valid: valid, steps_total: total}
}

pattern sweep_record(sid: Float, res: Struct, result_date: String) -> Struct {
  // Fix the accepted run: the sweep_result row (invariant 6) + the kv
  // mirror. The verdict compares against the previous recorded run per
  // the preregistration: the tempo delta <= 0.3 breaths/min AND the
  // power fraction ratio in [0.5; 2.0]. The first recorded run carries
  // the empty verdict — there is nothing to reproduce against yet.
  let prev = query("SELECT resonance_bpm, power_fraction FROM sweep_result ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [])
  let mut verdict = ""
  let mut delta = 0.0
  let mut ratio = 0.0
  let mut prev_bpm = 0.0
  if len(prev) > 0.0 {
    prev_bpm = to_float(prev[0].resonance_bpm)
    let prev_share = to_float(prev[0].power_fraction)
    delta = abs(res.resonance_bpm - prev_bpm)
    if prev_share > 0.0 {
      ratio = res.share / prev_share
    }
    if delta <= 0.3 and ratio >= 0.5 and ratio <= 2.0 {
      verdict = "reproducible"
    } else {
      verdict = "divergent"
    }
  }
  let _ = db_execute("INSERT INTO sweep_result (session_id, result_date, resonance_bpm, peak_freq_bpm, power_fraction, p_value, steps_valid, steps_total, prev_resonance_bpm, freq_delta_bpm, share_ratio, verdict) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)", [sid, result_date, res.resonance_bpm, res.peak_freq_bpm, res.share, res.p_value, res.steps_valid, res.steps_total, prev_bpm, delta, ratio, verdict])
  let _ = kv_set("resonance_bpm", to_string(res.resonance_bpm))
  let _ = kv_set("resonance_peak_freq", to_string(res.peak_freq_bpm))
  let _ = kv_set("resonance_share", to_string(res.share))
  let _ = kv_set("resonance_verdict", verdict)
  return {ok: true, resonance_bpm: res.resonance_bpm, peak_freq_bpm: res.peak_freq_bpm, share: res.share, p_value: res.p_value, steps_valid: res.steps_valid, steps_total: res.steps_total, verdict: verdict, freq_delta_bpm: delta, share_ratio: ratio}
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-END: store-core
pattern last_proposed_trial(local_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id, arm_id, day_window FROM trial WHERE status = 'proposed' AND trial_date = ? ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [local_date])
}

pattern close_stale_misses(local_date: String) -> Float {
  let stale = query("SELECT id FROM trial WHERE status = 'proposed' AND trial_date < ? AND arm_id IS NOT NULL", [local_date])
  let mut closed = 0.0
  each t in stale {
    let tid = t.id
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET status = 'missed', closed_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = ?", [tid])
    closed = closed + 1.0
  }
  return closed
}

pattern apply_answer(tid: Float, ans: Struct) -> String {
  if ans.kind == "prediction" {
    let rows = query("SELECT prediction_depth FROM trial WHERE id = ? AND status = 'proposed'", [tid])
    if len(rows) == 0.0 {
      return "no-open-trial"
    }
    if rows[0].prediction_depth != 0.0 {
      return "prediction-kept"
    }
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET prediction_depth = ? WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    // Н2-13: the context row is written AT THE RESPONSE TIME (the
    // probe-time write, the context module's decision 1) — blind until
    // the first response row opens the read (invariant 2); the sleep
    // sentinel -1.0 when s: has not been seen (never a fabricated 0;
    // a later s: in the batch updates the row in place).
    let _ = ensure_context_row(tid, 0 - 1.0)
    return "prediction"
  }
  if ans.kind == "moment" {
    let guard = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM response WHERE trial_id = ? AND kind = 'moment'", [tid])
    if guard[0].n > 0.0 {
      return "moment-kept"
    }
    let row = {trial_id: tid, kind: "moment", depth: ans.value, details: "telegram m:"}
    let _ = db_insert("response", row)
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET moment_value = ?, moment_present = 1, moment_source = 'subjective', status = 'completed' WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    let _ = compute_reward(tid)
    let _ = ensure_context_row(tid, 0 - 1.0)
    return "moment"
  }
  // Н2-13: the optional sleep context — the value lands in the trial's
  // context row (in place when one exists, else a fresh row); the row
  // stays BLIND until the first response row (the read guard).
  if ans.kind == "sleep" {
    let rows = query("SELECT id FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [tid])
    if len(rows) == 0.0 {
      return "no-open-trial"
    }
    let ctx = query("SELECT id FROM context WHERE trial_id = ? ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [tid])
    if len(ctx) > 0.0 {
      let _ = db_execute("UPDATE context SET sleep_quality = ? WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, ctx[0].id])
    } else {
      let _ = collect_context(tid, now_unix(), ans.value)
    }
    return "sleep"
  }
  // Н2-12: the full-reward components (ADR-0001 — the formula is
  // closed, only the INPUTS arrive). The guard rides the presence
  // flag (fill an untouched default exactly once — the prediction
  // precedent); the reward RECOMPUTES as the normalized weighted sum
  // of the present components on every new one, idempotently. A late
  // component on a closed (missed/completed) trial is legal: the flag
  // flips, the reward recomputes, the status stays as the window left
  // it (no backdating — the bandit's own predicate decides what
  // counts).
  if ans.kind == "next_day" {
    let rows = query("SELECT next_day_present FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [tid])
    if len(rows) == 0.0 {
      return "no-open-trial"
    }
    if rows[0].next_day_present == 1.0 {
      return "next_day-kept"
    }
    let row = {trial_id: tid, kind: "next_day", depth: ans.value, details: "telegram nd:"}
    let _ = db_insert("response", row)
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET next_day_value = ?, next_day_present = 1 WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    let _ = compute_reward(tid)
    return "next_day"
  }
  if ans.kind == "action" {
    let rows = query("SELECT action_present FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [tid])
    if len(rows) == 0.0 {
      return "no-open-trial"
    }
    if rows[0].action_present == 1.0 {
      return "action-kept"
    }
    let row = {trial_id: tid, kind: "action", depth: ans.value, details: "telegram act:"}
    let _ = db_insert("response", row)
    let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET action_value = ?, action_present = 1 WHERE id = ?", [ans.value, tid])
    let _ = compute_reward(tid)
    return "action"
  }
  let rows2 = query("SELECT free_note FROM trial WHERE id = ?", [tid])
  let mut note = ""
  if len(rows2) > 0.0 {
    note = rows2[0].free_note
  }
  let joined = note + " | " + escape_html(ans.text)
  let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET free_note = ? WHERE id = ?", [joined, tid])
  return "note"
}

// Н2-13: the probe-time context write, once per trial — a repeated
// response (prediction after the moment, a note, a second drain) does
// NOT add a second row; the sleep sentinel -1.0 means «не отвечено»
// (the silent zero is forbidden). The blindness of the row is the
// context module's own contract (the read guard).
pattern ensure_context_row(tid: Float, sleep_quality: Float) -> Float {
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM context WHERE trial_id = ?", [tid])
  if rows[0].n > 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  return collect_context(tid, now_unix(), sleep_quality)
}

// ── H2-07-SPECTRAL-START (byte-mirrored into app.mlog telegram-core) ────
// The M2 projection source (Н2-07, ADR-0001): with a valid practice RR
// series the trial's moment is written by the SPECTRAL source — the
// power fraction in the band around the dominant peak (the honest
// resonance measure per the concept; the №591 builtins do the math,
// sin/cos are absent from the 0.30.0 grammar). The subjective scales
// stay the fallback: their drain path above is guarded by the ANY-moment
// response count, so an existing projection is never silently
// overwritten, and the projection carries the declared PRIORITY over an
// earlier subjective row (both rows remain in response — nothing is
// lost; the trial fixes the source actually used).

pattern moment_spectral_from_rr(rr_ms: List) -> Struct {
  // A practice RR series -> the spectral verdict. Loud refusal on a
  // short or degraded series (the language floor is 12 points,
  // probe-pinned) — the fallback stays untouched, never a fabricated 0.
  if len(rr_ms) < 12.0 {
    return {ok: false, share: 0.0, peak_hz: 0.0, reason: "RR-ряд короче 12 точек: " + to_string(len(rr_ms))}
  }
  let ts = sweep_rr_times(rr_ms)
  let spec = lomb_scargle(ts, rr_ms)
  let pk = spectral_peak(spec)
  if pk.degraded == true {
    return {ok: false, share: 0.0, peak_hz: 0.0, reason: "спектр деградировал: точек " + to_string(len(rr_ms))}
  }
  return {ok: true, share: pk.power_fraction, peak_hz: pk.freq, reason: ""}
}

pattern moment_spectral_write(tid: Float, share: Float, peak_hz: Float) -> Float {
  // The guarded projection write: once per trial (a repeated projection
  // is refused loudly by the caller contract — 0.0, rows untouched).
  // The response row makes the write visible to the drain's ANY-moment
  // guard, so the subjective fallback can never silently replace it.
  let guard = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM response WHERE trial_id = ? AND kind = 'moment' AND details LIKE 'spectral%'", [tid])
  if guard[0].n > 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let row = {trial_id: tid, kind: "moment", depth: share, details: "spectral projection: peak " + to_string(peak_hz) + " Hz"}
  let _ = db_insert("response", row)
  let _ = db_execute("UPDATE trial SET moment_value = ?, moment_present = 1, moment_source = 'spectral', status = 'completed' WHERE id = ?", [share, tid])
  return 1.0
}
// ── H2-07-SPECTRAL-END ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

pattern process_updates(updates: List<public, trusted>, chat_id: String<public, trusted>, now_ts: Float, tz_offset_hours: Float, offset: Float, with_report: Bool) -> Unit {
  // Н2-10: an answer belongs to the trial of the window its MESSAGE fell
  // into (message.date, the Telegram server clock), not to the window of
  // the tick that happens to drain it; a message without a date falls
  // back to the tick moment. The close threshold is the end of the window
  // (window_date of now), so an early manual /fire never closes a live trial.
  // The D2-family posture: the drain is a BARE each (db effects inside
  // the loop are the m0_row-proven shape), every diagnostic lives in
  // counters, ONE summary print after the loop. The chat filter
  // compares SANITIZED projections; the untrusted raw never branches.
  // Н2-11: with_report=false silences the counters message for the
  // 21:30 collect tick — the report stays the 02:00 closing tick's
  // signature; the collect tick speaks only through its ONE request.
  let mut processed = 0.0
  let mut predictions = 0.0
  let mut moments = 0.0
  let mut skipped = 0.0
  let mut last_id = 0 - 1.0
  each u in updates {
    last_id = json_get(u, "update_id", 0.0)
    let chat = to_string(json_get(u, "message.chat.id", 0.0))
    if escape_html(chat) == escape_html(chat_id) {
      let text = json_get(u, "message.text", "")
      if escape_html(text) != "" {
        let ans = parse_chat_text(text)
        // Н2-13: the honesty-valve report on request — the command is
        // answered directly, no trial routing; the text is the
        // escape_html-wrapped SSOT report (the chat form).
        if ans.kind == "report" {
          let _ = send_message(chat_id, honesty_report_chat())
          processed = processed + 1.0
        } else {
        // Н2-12: the full-reward answers bind by the PENDING QUESTION,
        // not by the message window — the bot asks about ONE trial per
        // question kind (the kv pendings are set by the morning ask and
        // cleared on a successful write), so «ответ о вчерашней пробе»
        // and «о трёхдневной давности» never cross. A spontaneous
        // answer with no pending question is skipped, never guessed.
        let mut tid = 0.0
        let mut routed = false
        if ans.kind == "next_day" {
          let p = to_float_or(kv_get("nd_pending_trial"), 0.0)
          if p > 0.0 {
            tid = p
            routed = true
          }
        } else {
          if ans.kind == "action" {
            let p2 = to_float_or(kv_get("act_pending_trial"), 0.0)
            if p2 > 0.0 {
              tid = p2
              routed = true
            }
          } else {
            let mut msg_ts = json_get(u, "message.date", 0.0)
            if msg_ts <= 0.0 {
              msg_ts = now_ts
            }
            if ans.kind == "sleep" {
              // The sleep note binds to the window's trial in ANY
              // status (the completed trial's day context arrives late).
              let open = latest_window_trial(window_date(msg_ts, tz_offset_hours))
              if len(open) > 0.0 {
                tid = open[0].id
                routed = true
              }
            } else {
              let open = last_proposed_trial(window_date(msg_ts, tz_offset_hours))
              if len(open) > 0.0 {
                tid = open[0].id
                routed = true
              }
            }
          }
        }
        if routed == true {
          let applied = apply_answer(tid, ans)
          if applied == "prediction" {
            predictions = predictions + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "moment" {
            moments = moments + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "next_day" {
            moments = moments + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
            let _ = kv_set("nd_pending_trial", "0")
          }
          if applied == "action" {
            moments = moments + 1.0
            processed = processed + 1.0
            let _ = kv_set("act_pending_trial", "0")
          }
          if applied == "note" {
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "sleep" {
            processed = processed + 1.0
          }
          if applied == "no-open-trial" {
            skipped = skipped + 1.0
          }
        } else {
          skipped = skipped + 1.0
        }
        }
      } else {
        skipped = skipped + 1.0
      }
    } else {
      skipped = skipped + 1.0
    }
  }
  // The offset advances AFTER the batch; a crash before the kv_set
  // replays the batch into the idempotent guards (design note 4).
  if last_id >= 0.0 {
    let next_offset = last_id + 1.0
    if next_offset != offset {
      let _ = kv_set("tg_offset", to_string(next_offset))
    }
  }
  let closed = close_stale_misses(window_date(now_ts, tz_offset_hours))
  if with_report == true {
    let _ = send_message(chat_id, format_report(processed, closed, predictions, moments))
  }
  print("[telegram] drain: processed=" + to_string(processed) + " closed=" + to_string(closed) + " predictions=" + to_string(predictions) + " moments=" + to_string(moments) + " skipped=" + to_string(skipped))
}

pattern has_job(expr: String, target: String) -> Bool {
  // each over the snapshot: the while+len shape misconverges when the
  // body can reach cron_remove (the worklog probe, the new D2-family
  // symptom) — this pass must stay removal-free AND each-shaped.
  let jobs = cron_list()
  let mut found = false
  each j in jobs {
    if j.cron_expr == expr and j.prompt == target {
      found = true
    }
  }
  return found
}

pattern setup_register() -> Unit {
  // The D2-family posture: NO prints and NO mixed statements inside the
  // loop bodies — the stale sweep runs as a bare each, the add phase
  // runs through precomputed flags, ONE summary print after everything
  // (the probe: variant A misconverges, variant B converges).
  // Н2-11: THREE jobs — the morning proposal (07:00), the evening
  // collect request (21:30) and the window-closing drain (02:00); a
  // KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET change folds every expression and the stale
  // sweep removes the outdated copies by prompt.
  // Н2-13: the FOURTH job — the honesty valve's weekly report
  // (Monday 09:30 local).
  let off = to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))
  let morning = cron_expr_for(420.0, off)
  let collect = cron_expr_for(1290.0, off)
  let evening = cron_expr_for(120.0, off)
  let weekly = cron_expr_for(570.0, off)
  let jobs = cron_list()
  // №706 (mlog 0.33.1): cron_list rows flow as private (prompt/payload
  // are user-authored content — the №689 whole-struct fail-closed
  // posture), and cron_remove/cron_run are decision sinks (№391) — the
  // id takes the sanctioned redact bridge: redact(id,
  // "secrets") sheds the label and passes the id string through
  // unchanged (probe-pinned on 0.33.1: real ids are "cron_<ts>_<n>"
  // strings, the value survives byte-exact); the
  // derived count in the summary print rides the escape_html bridge.
  each j in jobs {
    if j.prompt == "tg_morning_tick" and j.cron_expr != morning {
      let _ = cron_remove(redact(j.id, "secrets"))
    }
    if j.prompt == "tg_collect_tick" and j.cron_expr != collect {
      let _ = cron_remove(redact(j.id, "secrets"))
    }
    if j.prompt == "tg_evening_tick" and j.cron_expr != evening {
      let _ = cron_remove(redact(j.id, "secrets"))
    }
    if j.prompt == "tg_weekly_tick" and j.cron_expr != weekly {
      let _ = cron_remove(redact(j.id, "secrets"))
    }
  }
  let add_m = has_job(morning, "tg_morning_tick") == false
  if add_m == true {
    let _ = cron_add(morning, "tg_morning_tick")
  }
  let add_c = has_job(collect, "tg_collect_tick") == false
  if add_c == true {
    let _ = cron_add(collect, "tg_collect_tick")
  }
  let add_e = has_job(evening, "tg_evening_tick") == false
  if add_e == true {
    let _ = cron_add(evening, "tg_evening_tick")
  }
  let add_w = has_job(weekly, "tg_weekly_tick") == false
  if add_w == true {
    let _ = cron_add(weekly, "tg_weekly_tick")
  }
  // VM defect #52 (minimal repro m6b): TWO print-ifs reading flags after
  // executed effect-call if-bodies miscompile on the serve VM lane — the
  // first /setup against an EMPTY store throws [TYPE_MISMATCH] Struct Eq
  // Bool (one pair is clean; the interpreter test lane never sees it, so
  // this suite stays green either way). The registration log is therefore
  // ONE flat summary print — the shape rig-validated clean on the full
  // setup_register body (m7full: 3/3 first-hit clean on an empty store).
  // mlog 0.34.1: print is a №316-class sink requiring public clearance;
  // the env-derived window strings carry 'private, trusted' — the
  // sanctioned redact bridge (№689) sheds the label, the value passes
  // through unchanged (probe-pinned on v0.34.1).
  print(redact("[telegram] cron setup: morning=" + morning + " collect=" + collect + " evening=" + evening + " weekly=" + weekly + " jobs=" + escape_html(to_string(len(cron_list()))), "secrets"))
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-END: db-cycle ─────────────────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: bandit-core (the signatures mirror
//    src/bandit/bandit.mlog; equality pinned by the worklog script) ────
// Thompson Normal-Normal on the decayed rewards, the 20% forced
// exploration floor, the seed contract. The entity constants below are
// byte-identical to the bandit module's.

entity reward_obs_std: Float = 0.25
entity decay_tau_days: Float = 60.0
entity explore_every: Float = 5.0

pattern today_unix() -> Float {
  return date_parse_iso(date_format_iso(now_unix()))
}

pattern decay_weight(age_days: Float) -> Float {
  if age_days <= decay_tau_days {
    return 1.0
  }
  return exp((decay_tau_days - age_days) / decay_tau_days)
}

pattern arm_posterior(arm_id: Float, prior_mean: Float, prior_std: Float) -> List {
  let mut s0 = prior_std
  if s0 <= 0.0 {
    s0 = 1.0
  }
  let rows = query("SELECT reward, trial_date FROM trial WHERE arm_id = ? AND status = 'completed' AND (moment_present = 1 OR next_day_present = 1 OR action_present = 1)", [arm_id])
  let today = today_unix()
  let mut wsum = 0.0
  let mut xsum = 0.0
  each r in rows {
    let mut age = date_diff_days(today, date_parse_iso(r.trial_date))
    if age < 0.0 {
      age = 0.0
    }
    let w = decay_weight(age)
    wsum = wsum + w
    xsum = xsum + w * r.reward
  }
  let inv0 = 1.0 / (s0 * s0)
  let invr = 1.0 / (reward_obs_std * reward_obs_std)
  let precision = inv0 + wsum * invr
  let mean = (prior_mean * inv0 + xsum * invr) / precision
  let sd = 1.0 / sqrt(precision)
  return [mean, sd, wsum]
}

pattern bandit_pick(seed: Float) -> Struct {
  let arms = query("SELECT id, name, prior_mean, prior_std FROM arm WHERE active = 1 ORDER BY id", [])
  let k = len(arms)
  if k == 0.0 {
    return {arm_id: 0.0, mode: "empty", theta: 0.0}
  }
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM trial WHERE arm_id IS NOT NULL", [])
  let n = rows[0].n
  if to_int(n / explore_every) * explore_every == n {
    let step = to_int(n / explore_every)
    let kk = to_int(k)
    let idx = step - kk * to_int(step / kk)
    let arm = arms[idx]
    return {arm_id: arm.id, mode: "explore", theta: 0.0}
  }
  random_seed(seed)
  let mut i = 0.0
  let mut best_id = 0.0
  let mut best_theta = 0.0
  let mut first = true
  while i < k {
    let arm = arms[i]
    let post = arm_posterior(arm.id, arm.prior_mean, arm.prior_std)
    let theta = post[0] + post[1] * normal_sample(0.0, 1.0)
    if first == true {
      best_id = arm.id
      best_theta = theta
      first = false
    }
    if theta > best_theta {
      best_id = arm.id
      best_theta = theta
    }
    i = i + 1.0
  }
  return {arm_id: best_id, mode: "thompson", theta: best_theta}
}

pattern bandit_propose(trial_date: String, seed: Float) -> Float {
  // Н2-08 day guard: a proposal is one per calendar day — a repeated
  // tick re-shows the existing trial instead of a second decision.
  let existing = query("SELECT id FROM trial WHERE trial_date = ? AND arm_id IS NOT NULL ORDER BY id LIMIT 1", [trial_date])
  if len(existing) > 0.0 {
    return existing[0].id
  }
  let pick = bandit_pick(seed)
  if pick.arm_id == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  let arm = query("SELECT id, day_window FROM arm WHERE id = ?", [pick.arm_id])
  if len(arm) == 0.0 {
    return 0.0
  }
  // Н2-12: the proposal carries the ACTIVE note's id — the «Нота:»
  // line stops being permanently empty (the trial joins note by id in
  // morning_proposal_row). No note row — the key stays absent (SQL
  // NULL default), never a fabricated 0 (the FK-target row does not
  // exist); two branches instead of a nullable field in one struct
  // (the language has no nullable struct fields).
  let note = query("SELECT id FROM note WHERE active = 1 ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [])
  if len(note) > 0.0 {
    let row = {trial_date: trial_date, day_window: arm[0].day_window, arm_id: pick.arm_id, note_id: note[0].id}
    return db_insert("trial", row)
  }
  let row = {trial_date: trial_date, day_window: arm[0].day_window, arm_id: pick.arm_id}
  return db_insert("trial", row)
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: bandit-core
// ── APP-MIRROR-START: arms-seed (byte-identical to
//    src/arms/arms.mlog §arms-seed) ─────────────────────────────────────

entity kamerton_arms: List = [
  {name: "breath-resonance-morning", group_name: "Резонансное дыхание", day_window: "morning", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.6, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Lehrer & Gevirtz 2014 (Front Psychol 5:753): resonance-frequency HRV biofeedback, robust baroreflex effects"},
  {name: "breath-resonance-evening", group_name: "Резонансное дыхание", day_window: "evening", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.6, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Lehrer & Gevirtz 2014 (Front Psychol 5:753): resonance-frequency HRV biofeedback, robust baroreflex effects"},
  {name: "woop-morning", group_name: "Имплементационные намерения", day_window: "morning", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.6, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Gollwitzer & Sheeran 2006 (Adv Exp Soc Psychol 38): meta-analysis of 94 studies, d ~ 0.65"},
  {name: "woop-evening", group_name: "Имплементационные намерения", day_window: "evening", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.6, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Gollwitzer & Sheeran 2006 (Adv Exp Soc Psychol 38): meta-analysis of 94 studies, d ~ 0.65"},
  {name: "mental-rehearsal-morning", group_name: "Ментальная репетиция", day_window: "morning", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.5, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Driskell, Copper & Moran 1994 (J Appl Psychol 79(4)): mental practice meta-analysis, moderate effect, decays without physical practice"},
  {name: "mental-rehearsal-evening", group_name: "Ментальная репетиция", day_window: "evening", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.5, prior_std: 0.15, source: "Driskell, Copper & Moran 1994 (J Appl Psychol 79(4)): mental practice meta-analysis, moderate effect, decays without physical practice"},
  {name: "focusing-morning", group_name: "Фокусинг", day_window: "morning", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.45, prior_std: 0.2, source: "Hendricks 2002 (The Focusing-oriented client): experiential review, small-N studies, mixed quality — wide prior"},
  {name: "focusing-evening", group_name: "Фокусинг", day_window: "evening", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.45, prior_std: 0.2, source: "Hendricks 2002 (The Focusing-oriented client): experiential review, small-N studies, mixed quality — wide prior"},
  {name: "yoga-nidra-morning", group_name: "Йога-нидра", day_window: "morning", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.45, prior_std: 0.2, source: "Moszeik, von Oertzen & Günther 2022 (Current Psychology): Yoga Nidra effects on stress, sleep, well-being — moderate, wide prior"},
  {name: "yoga-nidra-evening", group_name: "Йога-нидра", day_window: "evening", duration_min: 10.0, prior_mean: 0.45, prior_std: 0.2, source: "Moszeik, von Oertzen & Günther 2022 (Current Psychology): Yoga Nidra effects on stress, sleep, well-being — moderate, wide prior"}
]

// Seed the arm library. Idempotent by construction: a UNIQUE index on
// name plus INSERT OR IGNORE — a repeated run changes nothing.
//
// WHY UNROLLED STATEMENTS (§2, declared loudly): the mlog D2 defect
// (declared in Kamerton issue #24; verified on v0.28.1 AND v0.28.2 by
// mutation probes) mis-executes loops whose body is a bare call — one
// iteration, and in a test body the tail after such a loop is silently
// cut (vacuously green). Assignment-body loops are full, but the
// trigger surface is not fully mapped (the probeprint case differs
// from the db_execute case), so the discipline here is: NO loops in
// test bodies at all until the language naryads land (Metalogos-
// №597/№598 → v0.28.3). A loop-driven seed would silently insert only
// the first arm, so the seed is unrolled into sequential statements
// and pinned to the kamerton_arms entity list by the per-arm VALUES
// LEFT JOIN verification test (loop-free); the JSON mirror is pinned
// to the same list. Divergence of any copy is a loud test failure.

pattern seed_arms() -> Float {
  db_execute("CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_arm_name_unique ON arm(name)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('breath-resonance-morning', 'Резонансное дыхание', 'morning', 10, 0.6, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('breath-resonance-evening', 'Резонансное дыхание', 'evening', 10, 0.6, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('woop-morning', 'Имплементационные намерения', 'morning', 10, 0.6, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('woop-evening', 'Имплементационные намерения', 'evening', 10, 0.6, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('mental-rehearsal-morning', 'Ментальная репетиция', 'morning', 10, 0.5, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('mental-rehearsal-evening', 'Ментальная репетиция', 'evening', 10, 0.5, 0.15)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('focusing-morning', 'Фокусинг', 'morning', 10, 0.45, 0.2)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('focusing-evening', 'Фокусинг', 'evening', 10, 0.45, 0.2)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('yoga-nidra-morning', 'Йога-нидра', 'morning', 10, 0.45, 0.2)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO arm (name, group_name, day_window, duration_min, prior_mean, prior_std) VALUES ('yoga-nidra-evening', 'Йога-нидра', 'evening', 10, 0.45, 0.2)")
  // Н2-09: the practice DELIVERY — the proposal must tell what to do,
  // not just name the hand (the M1-window gap: the trial asked for a
  // prediction with no practice content anywhere). One 10-minute
  // instruction per methodology group, grounded in the SAME literature
  // sources as the arms above; the proposal joins this table by
  // arm.group_name. Idempotent like the arm seed: UNIQUE(group_name)
  // plus INSERT OR IGNORE. Loop-free by the D2 discipline (unrolled,
  // like the arm seed above). The bodies carry no quote characters —
  // the SQL literals stay plain; a missing or empty row degrades LOUD
  // in the proposal (the NULLIF fallback, see morning_proposal_row).
  db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS practice_text (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, group_name TEXT, body TEXT, active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))")
  db_execute("CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_practice_text_group_unique ON practice_text(group_name)")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO practice_text (group_name, body) VALUES ('Резонансное дыхание', 'Сядь ровно, таймер на 10 минут. Дыши через нос, медленно и ровно: вдох около 5 секунд, выдох около 5 секунд — примерно 5–6 циклов в минуту, без усилия. Живот мягко уходит вперёд на вдохе. Держи ровный ритм: сбился — спокойно возвращайся к счёту. Это резонансная зона 4.5–6.5 вдохов в минуту, на ней дыхание и сердечный ритм входят в синхрон (Lehrer и Gevirtz, 2014).')")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO practice_text (group_name, body) VALUES ('Имплементационные намерения', 'Бумага и ручка, 10 минут по четырём шагам. W — желание: запиши важное и реальное желание на ближайшие дни. O — исход: 2–3 минуты живо представляй лучший результат его достижения. O — препятствие: честно назови внутреннее, что чаще всего мешает. P — план: собери формулу «если у меня …, то я …», подставь своё препятствие и своё действие, повтори про себя 2–3 раза (Оэттинген; Голвитцер и Ширан, 2006).')")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO practice_text (group_name, body) VALUES ('Ментальная репетиция', 'Выбери конкретный навык или предстоящее действие: выступление, разговор, движение. Первые 1–2 минуты — вживись в обстановку: где, что вокруг, кто рядом. Затем проиграй действие от начала до конца изнутри, своими глазами, в реальном темпе. Трудное место пройди отдельно 2–3 раза в исправленном варианте. Финал — одна уверенная полная прогонка без остановок. Репетиция дополняет физическую практику, а не заменяет её (Driskell, Copper и Moran, 1994).')")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO practice_text (group_name, body) VALUES ('Фокусинг', 'Сядь удобно, 10 минут. Минута: пройди вниманием по телу — где сейчас самое заметное ощущение. 2–3 минуты: не меняй его, просто признай — здравствуй, я тебя вижу. Спроси внутри: о чём это? Не отвечай умом — жди телесного отклика, каким бы медленным он ни был. Всё, что придёт, признай без спора. Закончи вопросом: чего тебе нужно? — и спокойно выходи. Здесь ничего не надо добиваться: важно только присутствие внимания (Gendlin; Hendricks, 2002).')")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO practice_text (group_name, body) VALUES ('Йога-нидра', 'Ляг на спину, руки чуть в стороны, глаза закрыты — держи лёгкую бодрость, не засыпай. Короткое намерение в настоящем времени, своими словами. Затем медленно пройди вниманием по телу: правая рука, левая рука, ноги, туловище, лицо. Дальше пары ощущений: тяжесть — лёгкость, тепло — прохлада. Потом просто наблюдай дыхание, не считая. В конце повтори намерение и сделай 2–3 глубоких вдоха, вставай медленно. Сжатая форма на 10 минут (Moszeik и соавт., 2022).')")
  // Н2-12: the note-goal — ONE row, the owner's formulation VERBATIM
  // from the concept (docs/concept-v2.md, «Нота и принцип»); the fixed
  // id keeps the seed idempotent (INSERT OR IGNORE) across re-runs and
  // the formulation is the OWNER's text, not the executor's invention
  // (the naryad Шаг 0 defers the wording to the owner — the concept's
  // own sentence IS the owner's wording). bandit_propose joins the
  // trial to the ACTIVE note (the latest active row), so a future
  // re-wording is a data edit, never a code change.
  db_execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS note (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, body TEXT, active INTEGER DEFAULT '1', created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')))")
  db_execute("INSERT OR IGNORE INTO note (id, body, active) VALUES (1, 'Между тем, чего я хочу, и тем, что я делаю, нет зазора — и это видно по результату.', 1)")
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM arm", [])
  return rows[0].n
}

// ── APP-MIRROR-END: arms-seed ─────────────────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: miniapp-core (byte-identical to
//    src/miniapp/miniapp.mlog §miniapp-core) ────────────────────────────

// Mini App core (Н2-03): the token guard, the page literal and the
// practice-session writers. The page is served from the TRUSTED
// literal: read_file output carries 'public, untrusted' and the №391
// sink clearance refuses respond(read_file(...)) (probe n203-serve-1),
// so self-host/miniapp/index.html is the byte-pinned canon and this
// literal is its serving copy; the lockstep test in the miniapp module
// pins the byte equality.

// The token guard — PURE function (the test lane has no env gate): the
// route passes the allowlisted stored value and the SANITIZED provided
// one (the escape_html bridge over query_param — the repo's
// sanitize-then-decide convention; the deploy token charset is
// alphanumeric, so the bridge is exact). Fail-closed: an unconfigured
// token (empty stored value) denies everything.
pattern miniapp_check_token(stored: String, provided: String) -> Bool {
  if stored == "" {
    return false
  }
  return provided == stored
}

// The page literal — byte-pinned to self-host/miniapp/index.html (see
// the miniapp module tests). No external origin anywhere in the markup
// (invariant 7): inline CSS/JS only, same-origin fetches only.
pattern miniapp_html() -> String {
  return "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"ru\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Камертон — практики</title>\n<style>\n  :root { --bg:#0f1115; --fg:#e8e6e3; --dim:#9a9a93; --accent:#e8862c; --ok:#4f9d69; --err:#c94f4f; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; }\n  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n  nav { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\n  nav button { flex: 1; padding: 10px; background: #1a1d24; color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid #2a2e37; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 15px; }\n  nav button.on { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }\n  .screen { display: none; }\n  .screen.on { display: block; }\n  .card { background: #161920; border: 1px solid #2a2e37; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n  .circle { width: 160px; height: 160px; border-radius: 50%; background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%, #3a4152, #22262f); margin: 24px auto; }\n  .lbl { color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; }\n  .row { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-top: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n  button.act { padding: 10px 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--accent); color: #14100b; font-size: 15px; }\n  button.act.sec { background: #2a2e37; color: var(--fg); }\n  #status { font-size: 13px; color: var(--dim); min-height: 20px; margin-top: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  .ok { color: var(--ok); } .err { color: var(--err); }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Камертон</h1>\n<nav>\n  <button id=\"tab-pacer\" class=\"on\" onclick=\"show('pacer')\">Пейсер</button>\n  <button id=\"tab-ppg\" onclick=\"show('ppg')\">Пульс</button>\n</nav>\n\n<section id=\"screen-pacer\" class=\"screen on\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <div class=\"circle\" id=\"pacer-circle\"></div>\n    <p class=\"lbl\" id=\"pacer-phase\">&nbsp;</p>\n    <p class=\"lbl\">Темп: <b id=\"pacer-tempo\">5.5</b> вдохов/мин (диапазон 4.5–7.0, шаг 0.25)</p>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button class=\"act sec\" onclick=\"tempoDown()\">−</button>\n      <button class=\"act sec\" onclick=\"tempoUp()\">+</button>\n      <button class=\"act\" id=\"pacer-step-btn\" onclick=\"startStep()\">Старт шага (2 мин)</button>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lbl\" id=\"pacer-timer\">&nbsp;</p>\n    <p class=\"lbl\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ppg-during-step\"> писать пульс во время шагов — RR-сегмент на каждый темп (Н2-06)</label></p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <p class=\"lbl\">Журнал сессии (таблица practice_session, SQLite)</p>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button class=\"act\" onclick=\"openSession('pacer')\">Начать сессию</button>\n      <button class=\"act\" onclick=\"openSession('sweep')\">Начать протокол перебора</button>\n      <button class=\"act sec\" onclick=\"closeSession()\">Завершить</button>\n    </div>\n    <p id=\"pacer-marks\" class=\"lbl\"></p>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"screen-ppg\" class=\"screen\">\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <video id=\"ppg-video\" playsinline muted autoplay style=\"width:120px;height:120px;border-radius:50%;object-fit:cover;background:#22262f;display:block;margin:0 auto;\"></video>\n    <p class=\"lbl\" id=\"ppg-hint\">Палец на объектив камеры (или лицо в кадр). Кадры обрабатываются на устройстве и никуда не сохраняются — инвариант 7.</p>\n    <p class=\"lbl\" id=\"ppg-timer\">&nbsp;</p>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <button class=\"act\" id=\"ppg-start-btn\" onclick=\"ppgStart()\">Старт записи</button>\n      <button class=\"act sec\" id=\"ppg-stop-btn\" onclick=\"ppgStop()\" disabled>Стоп</button>\n      <button class=\"act sec\" id=\"ppg-save-btn\" onclick=\"ppgSave()\" disabled>Сохранить RR в сессию</button>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lbl\" id=\"ppg-summary\">&nbsp;</p>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<p id=\"status\"></p>\n\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n// Канал ADR-0002 (вариант «а», приватный туннель): страница отдаётся\n// маршрутом /miniapp программы Камертона; токен владельца передаётся в\n// каждом запросе (параметр t из адреса страницы). Наружу страница не\n// ходит: вся работа против того же origin, внешних ресурсов нет —\n// инвариант 7 (данные не покидают машину владельца).\nvar TOKEN = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get(\"t\") || \"\";\nvar sessionId = 0;\nvar marks = [];\n\nfunction show(name) {\n  var names = [\"pacer\", \"ppg\"];\n  for (var i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {\n    document.getElementById(\"screen-\" + names[i]).className = names[i] === name ? \"screen on\" : \"screen\";\n    document.getElementById(\"tab-\" + names[i]).className = names[i] === name ? \"on\" : \"\";\n  }\n}\n\nfunction status(msg, cls) {\n  var el = document.getElementById(\"status\");\n  el.textContent = msg;\n  el.className = cls || \"\";\n}\n\nfunction api(path, params) {\n  var q = new URLSearchParams(params || {});\n  q.set(\"t\", TOKEN);\n  return fetch(path + \"?\" + q.toString(), {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"X-CSRF-Token\": csrfToken() }\n  })\n    .then(function (r) {\n      return r.text().then(function (body) { return { code: r.status, body: body }; });\n    });\n}\n\n// CSRF-мидлварь сервера (double-submit): GET страницы выдаёт куку\n// _mlog_csrf, каждый POST обязан нести её значение в X-CSRF-Token.\n// TTL токена — 15 минут; истёкший/чужой токен отвечает 403 с «CSRF»\n// в теле — перезагружаем страницу (GET перевыпустит куку). Отметки\n// шагов пишутся инкрементально, поэтому перезагрузка теряет максимум\n// текущий неотмеченный шаг.\nfunction csrfToken() {\n  var m = document.cookie.match(/(?:^|;\\s*)_mlog_csrf=([^;]+)/);\n  return m ? m[1] : \"\";\n}\n\nfunction openSession(kind) {\n  api(\"/miniapp/session\", { kind: kind, tempo_bpm: String(tempo), steps_total: String(STEPS_TOTAL), arm_id: \"0\", trial_id: \"0\" })\n    .then(function (res) {\n      if (res.code === 403 && res.body.indexOf(\"CSRF\") >= 0) { location.reload(); return; }\n      if (res.code !== 200) { status(\"Отказ сервера: \" + res.code + \" \" + res.body, \"err\"); return; }\n      var d = JSON.parse(res.body);\n      sessionId = d.id;\n      marks = [];\n      document.getElementById(\"pacer-marks\").textContent = \"Сессия №\" + sessionId + \", шагов: 0\";\n      status(\"Сессия \" + sessionId + \" открыта: протокол \" + STEPS_TOTAL + \" шагов по 2 минуты\", \"ok\");\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Ошибка сети: \" + e, \"err\"); });\n}\n\n// ── Пейсер (Н2-04) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// Протокол концепции: перебор темпов 4.5–7.0 вдох/мин с шагом 0.25,\n// по две минуты на темп; отметка завершения шага пишется в сессию\n// инкрементально (писцы Н2-03). Чистая математика фазы вынесена в\n// pacerState — её пиннет скрипт-проверка против эталонной раскадки\n// (self-host/miniapp/test/pacer-test.mjs).\n// PacerEngine-START (маркер скрипт-проверки: источник математики)\nvar TEMPO_MIN = 4.5;\nvar TEMPO_MAX = 7.0;\nvar TEMPO_STEP = 0.25;\nvar STEP_MS = 120000;   // две минуты на темп — протокол концепции\nvar STEPS_TOTAL = 11;   // (7.0 − 4.5) / 0.25 + 1\n\n// Плавная синусоида: равные половины вдоха/выдоха, масштаб 0.10–1.00,\n// старт из середины (0.55) на вдохе. Никакого накопления дрейфа: фаза\n// всегда считается от времени старта шага, а не приращением.\nfunction pacerState(tempoBpm, tMs) {\n  var periodMs = 60000 / tempoBpm;\n  var phase = (tMs % periodMs) / periodMs;\n  var s = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * phase);\n  return {\n    periodMs: periodMs,\n    phase: phase,\n    dir: phase < 0.5 ? \"вдох\" : \"выдох\",\n    scale: 0.55 + 0.45 * s\n  };\n}\n// PacerEngine-END\n\nvar tempo = 5.5;\nvar stepRunning = false;\nvar stepStart = 0;\nvar stepNo = 0;\nvar rafId = 0;\n\nfunction tempoUp() {\n  tempo = Math.min(TEMPO_MAX, Math.round((tempo + TEMPO_STEP) * 100) / 100);\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-tempo\").textContent = tempo.toFixed(2);\n}\n\nfunction tempoDown() {\n  tempo = Math.max(TEMPO_MIN, Math.round((tempo - TEMPO_STEP) * 100) / 100);\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-tempo\").textContent = tempo.toFixed(2);\n}\n\nfunction startStep() {\n  if (stepRunning) { return; }\n  if (!sessionId) { status(\"Сначала начните сессию\", \"err\"); return; }\n  var wantPpg = document.getElementById(\"ppg-during-step\").checked;\n  if (wantPpg && ppgSampling) { status(\"Сначала остановите запись на вкладке «Пульс»\", \"err\"); return; }\n  stepRunning = true;\n  stepNo = marks.length + 1;\n  stepStart = performance.now();\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-step-btn\").disabled = true;\n  if (wantPpg) { sweepStepStart(); }\n  paceFrame();\n}\n\nfunction paceFrame() {\n  var t = performance.now() - stepStart;\n  if (t >= STEP_MS) {\n    finishStep();\n    return;\n  }\n  var st = pacerState(tempo, t);\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-circle\").style.transform = \"scale(\" + st.scale.toFixed(4) + \")\";\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-phase\").textContent = st.dir;\n  var left = Math.ceil((STEP_MS - t) / 1000);\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-timer\").textContent = \"Шаг \" + stepNo + \" · осталось \" + left + \" с\";\n  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(paceFrame);\n}\n\nfunction finishStep() {\n  stepRunning = false;\n  cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-circle\").style.transform = \"scale(0.55)\";\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-phase\").textContent = \"\\u00a0\";\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-timer\").textContent = \"\\u00a0\";\n  document.getElementById(\"pacer-step-btn\").disabled = false;\n  var rec = stepMark();\n  api(\"/miniapp/session/close\", {\n    id: String(sessionId),\n    steps_done: String(marks.length + 1),\n    step_marks: JSON.stringify(marks.concat([rec])),\n    rr_json: \"\",\n    rr_source: \"\"\n  })\n    .then(function (res) {\n      if (res.code === 403 && res.body.indexOf(\"CSRF\") >= 0) { location.reload(); return; }\n      if (res.code !== 200) { status(\"Отказ сервера: \" + res.code + \" \" + res.body, \"err\"); return; }\n      marks.push(rec);\n      document.getElementById(\"pacer-marks\").textContent = \"Сессия №\" + sessionId + \", шагов: \" + marks.length + \" · последний темп \" + tempo.toFixed(2);\n      if (rec.rr_reason !== \"\") {\n        status(\"Шаг \" + stepNo + \" (темп \" + tempo.toFixed(2) + \") записан, но пульс забракован: \" + rec.rr_reason, \"err\");\n      } else if (rec.rr.length) {\n        status(\"Шаг \" + stepNo + \" (темп \" + tempo.toFixed(2) + \") записан с RR (\" + rec.rr.length + \" интервалов) — смените темп и повторите\", \"ok\");\n      } else {\n        status(\"Шаг \" + stepNo + \" (темп \" + tempo.toFixed(2) + \") записан — смените темп и повторите\", \"ok\");\n      }\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Ошибка сети: \" + e, \"err\"); });\n}\n\nfunction closeSession() {\n  if (!sessionId) { status(\"Сессия не открыта\", \"err\"); return; }\n  api(\"/miniapp/session/close\", {\n    id: String(sessionId),\n    steps_done: String(marks.length),\n    step_marks: JSON.stringify(marks),\n    rr_json: rrBuffer.length ? JSON.stringify(rrBuffer) : \"\",\n    rr_source: rrBuffer.length ? \"ppg\" : \"\",\n    final: \"1\"\n  })\n    .then(function (res) {\n      if (res.code === 403 && res.body.indexOf(\"CSRF\") >= 0) { location.reload(); return; }\n      if (res.code !== 200) { status(\"Отказ сервера: \" + res.code + \" \" + res.body, \"err\"); return; }\n      var d = JSON.parse(res.body);\n      if (d.sweep && d.sweep.ok) {\n        var v = \"\";\n        if (d.sweep.verdict === \"reproducible\") { v = \" · повтор: воспроизведён\"; }\n        if (d.sweep.verdict === \"divergent\") { v = \" · повтор: РАСХОЖДЕНИЕ\"; }\n        status(\"Протокол принят: резонанс \" + d.sweep.resonance_bpm + \" вдох/мин, доля мощности \" + Math.round(d.sweep.share * 100) + \"%\" + v + \" — зафиксировано в sweep_result\", \"ok\");\n      } else if (d.sweep) {\n        status(\"Протокол не принят: \" + d.sweep.reason, \"err\");\n      } else {\n        status(\"Сессия \" + sessionId + \" закрыта: шагов \" + marks.length + (rrBuffer.length ? \", RR \" + rrBuffer.length : \"\"), \"ok\");\n      }\n      sessionId = 0; marks = []; rrBuffer = []; stepSamples = [];\n      sweepStopCam();\n      document.getElementById(\"pacer-marks\").textContent = \"\";\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Ошибка сети: \" + e, \"err\"); });\n}\n\n// ── PPG через камеру → RR-интервалы (Н2-05) ─────────────────────────────\n// Инвариант 7: кадры живут только в canvas на устройстве; наружу уходит\n// ТОЛЬКО итоговый RR-ряд с метками качества, по явному действию\n// владельца. Сырые кадры не сохраняются нигде — их некуда сохранять:\n// страница не имеет хранилища, кроме сессионного журнала RR.\n// PpgEngine-START (маркер скрипт-проверки: источник математики)\n// Дискретизация сигнала: {t: мс, v: 0..255 — средний зелёный канал\n// центральной области кадра}. Пайплайн: скользящая база (окно 1.5 с) →\n// AC-составляющая → эпохи по 10 с → пики (локальные максимумы выше\n// порога 0.6 амплитуды эпохи с рефрактерным окном 300 мс = верхний\n// предел 200 уд/мин) → RR = межпиковые интервалы.\n// Контроль качества эпохи: пиков ≥ 5; RR эпохи в [300, 2000] мс\n// (30–200 уд/мин); CV = std/mean ≤ 0.25; амплитуда ≥ 6× шумовой пол\n// (шум — медиана |Δv| соседних отсчётов). Отбракованные эпохи\n// считаются; итоговый отказ громкий: эпох < 2, брак > 50% или RR < 8.\nvar PPG_EPOCH_MS = 10000;\nvar PPG_BASELINE_MS = 1500;\nvar PPG_REFRACTORY_MS = 300;\nvar PPG_RR_MIN = 300;\nvar PPG_RR_MAX = 2000;\nvar PPG_CV_MAX = 0.25;\nvar PPG_AMPL_NOISE_X = 6.0;\n\nfunction ppgExtractRR(samples) {\n  var n = samples.length;\n  if (n < 2) {\n    return { rr: [], epochsTotal: 0, epochsRejected: 0, reason: \"слишком мало отсчётов\" };\n  }\n  // Скользящая база: среднее по отсчётам в окне ±PPG_BASELINE_MS/2.\n  var half = PPG_BASELINE_MS / 2;\n  var ac = new Array(n);\n  var j0 = 0, j1 = 0, sum = 0, cnt = 0;\n  for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    while (j1 < n && samples[j1].t <= samples[i].t + half) { sum += samples[j1].v; cnt++; j1++; }\n    while (j0 < n && samples[j0].t < samples[i].t - half) { sum -= samples[j0].v; cnt--; j0++; }\n    ac[i] = { t: samples[i].t, v: samples[i].v - sum / cnt };\n  }\n  // Шумовой пол: медиана |Δv| соседних отсчётов.\n  var diffs = [];\n  for (var i = 1; i < n; i++) { diffs.push(Math.abs(ac[i].v - ac[i - 1].v)); }\n  diffs.sort(function (a, b) { return a - b; });\n  var noise = diffs[Math.floor(diffs.length / 2)] || 0.001;\n  // Эпохи по времени.\n  var t0 = samples[0].t, tEnd = samples[n - 1].t;\n  var epochs = [];\n  for (var e = t0; e < tEnd; e += PPG_EPOCH_MS) { epochs.push({ from: e, to: e + PPG_EPOCH_MS }); }\n  var rr = [];\n  var rejected = 0;\n  for (var k = 0; k < epochs.length; k++) {\n    var ep = epochs[k];\n    var idx = [];\n    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) { if (ac[i].t >= ep.from && ac[i].t < ep.to) { idx.push(i); } }\n    if (idx.length < 10) { rejected++; continue; }\n    var lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity;\n    for (var i = 0; i < idx.length; i++) {\n      var v = ac[idx[i]].v;\n      if (v < lo) lo = v;\n      if (v > hi) hi = v;\n    }\n    var ampl = hi - lo;\n    if (ampl < PPG_AMPL_NOISE_X * noise) { rejected++; continue; }\n    var thr = lo + 0.6 * ampl;\n    var peaks = [];\n    var lastPeakT = -Infinity;\n    for (var i = 1; i < idx.length - 1; i++) {\n      var t = ac[idx[i]].t, v = ac[idx[i]].v;\n      if (v > thr && v >= ac[idx[i - 1]].v && v >= ac[idx[i + 1]].v && t - lastPeakT >= PPG_REFRACTORY_MS) {\n        peaks.push(t); lastPeakT = t;\n      }\n    }\n    if (peaks.length < 5) { rejected++; continue; }\n    var okEpoch = true;\n    var epRR = [];\n    for (var i = 1; i < peaks.length; i++) {\n      var d = peaks[i] - peaks[i - 1];\n      if (d < PPG_RR_MIN || d > PPG_RR_MAX) { okEpoch = false; break; }\n      epRR.push(d);\n    }\n    if (!okEpoch) { rejected++; continue; }\n    var mean = epRR.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + b; }, 0) / epRR.length;\n    var vari = epRR.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + (b - mean) * (b - mean); }, 0) / epRR.length;\n    var cv = Math.sqrt(vari) / mean;\n    if (cv > PPG_CV_MAX) { rejected++; continue; }\n    for (var i = 0; i < epRR.length; i++) { rr.push(epRR[i]); }\n  }\n  var epochsTotal = epochs.length;\n  return { rr: rr, epochsTotal: epochsTotal, epochsRejected: rejected, reason: \"\" };\n}\n\n// Громкий отказ сборки RR: возвращает строку отказа или пустую строку.\nfunction ppgQualityRefusal(ex) {\n  if (ex.epochsTotal < 2) { return \"брак: запись короче двух эпох (\" + ex.epochsTotal + \")\"; }\n  var share = ex.epochsRejected / ex.epochsTotal;\n  if (share > 0.5) { return \"брак: отбраковано эпох \" + ex.epochsRejected + \" из \" + ex.epochsTotal + \" — сигнала пульса нет\"; }\n  if (ex.rr.length < 8) { return \"брак: восстановлено RR \" + ex.rr.length + \" (< 8)\"; }\n  return \"\";\n}\n// PpgEngine-END\n\n// ── Протокол перебора (Н2-06) ───────────────────────────────────────────\n// SweepEngine-START (маркер скрипт-проверки: сборка RR-сегментов)\n// Каждому шагу пейсера — свой RR-сегмент: камера пишет пульс на протяжении\n// шага (инвариант 7: кадры умирают в canvas, наружу идёт только итоговый\n// RR), на финише сегмент проходит QC движка Н2-05 и попадает в отметку\n// {step, tempo_bpm, rr, rr_reason}. Сервер считает спектры билтинами\n// Ломба–Скаргла (№591), фиксирует резонанс в sweep_result и kv; анализ\n// запускается только финальным закрытием сессии (final=1).\nvar stepSamples = [];\nvar stepPpgOn = false;   // семплирование текущего шага идёт\n\nfunction sweepStepStart() {\n  ppgStart_ = performance.now();\n  stepSamples = [];\n  if (ppgStream) { stepPpgOn = true; stepSampleFrame(); return; }\n  if (!navigator.mediaDevices || !navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia) {\n    status(\"Камера недоступна: нужен защищённый контекст (https) — шаг пойдёт без пульса\", \"err\");\n    return;\n  }\n  navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: { facingMode: \"user\", width: 320, height: 240 }, audio: false })\n    .then(function (stream) {\n      ppgStream = stream;\n      var video = document.getElementById(\"ppg-video\");\n      video.srcObject = stream;\n      video.play();\n      stepPpgOn = true;\n      stepSampleFrame();\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Камера отказала громко: \" + e.name + \" — шаг пойдёт без пульса\", \"err\"); });\n}\n\nfunction stepSampleFrame() {\n  if (!stepPpgOn) { return; }\n  var video = document.getElementById(\"ppg-video\");\n  if (video.videoWidth > 0) {\n    ppgCtx.drawImage(video, 8, 8, 16, 16, 0, 0, 8, 8);\n    var d = ppgCtx.getImageData(0, 0, 8, 8).data;\n    var sum = 0;\n    for (var i = 0; i < d.length; i += 4) { sum += d[i + 1]; }\n    stepSamples.push({ t: performance.now() - ppgStart_, v: sum / (d.length / 4) });\n  }\n  requestAnimationFrame(stepSampleFrame);\n}\n\nfunction stepMark() {\n  // Отметка шага: RR-сегмент (если пульс писался) едет в отметке; брак\n  // едет громко в rr_reason — протокол продолжается, сервер считает\n  // шаг негодным. Поле rr присутствует ВСЕГДА — сервер отличает отметку\n  // Н2-06 от старого формата по наличию ключа.\n  var rec = { step: stepNo, tempo_bpm: tempo, rr: [], rr_reason: \"\" };\n  if (stepPpgOn) {\n    stepPpgOn = false;\n    var ex = ppgExtractRR(stepSamples);\n    var refusal = ppgQualityRefusal(ex);\n    if (refusal !== \"\") { rec.rr_reason = refusal; }\n    else { rec.rr = ex.rr; }\n    stepSamples = [];\n  }\n  return rec;\n}\n\nfunction sweepStopCam() {\n  // Камера протокола гасится вместе с сессией; если вкладка «Пульс»\n  // сейчас ведёт свою запись — её стрим не трогаем.\n  if (ppgStream && !ppgSampling) {\n    var tracks = ppgStream.getTracks();\n    for (var i = 0; i < tracks.length; i++) { tracks[i].stop(); }\n    ppgStream = null;\n  }\n}\n// SweepEngine-END\n\nvar rrBuffer = [];\nvar ppgStream = null;\nvar ppgSampling = false;\nvar ppgStart_ = 0;\nvar ppgCanvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\nppgCanvas.width = 32; ppgCanvas.height = 32;\nvar ppgCtx = ppgCanvas.getContext(\"2d\", { willReadFrequently: true });\nvar ppgSamples = [];\n\nfunction ppgStart() {\n  if (ppgSampling) { return; }\n  if (!navigator.mediaDevices || !navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia) {\n    status(\"Камера недоступна: нужен защищённый контекст (https) — канал ADR-0002 (а) его даёт, http-закладка нет\", \"err\");\n    return;\n  }\n  navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: { facingMode: \"user\", width: 320, height: 240 }, audio: false })\n    .then(function (stream) {\n      ppgStream = stream;\n      var video = document.getElementById(\"ppg-video\");\n      video.srcObject = stream;\n      video.play();\n      ppgSamples = [];\n      rrBuffer = [];\n      ppgSampling = true;\n      ppgStart_ = performance.now();\n      document.getElementById(\"ppg-start-btn\").disabled = true;\n      document.getElementById(\"ppg-stop-btn\").disabled = false;\n      document.getElementById(\"ppg-save-btn\").disabled = true;\n      document.getElementById(\"ppg-summary\").textContent = \"\";\n      ppgSampleFrame();\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Камера отказала громко: \" + e.name, \"err\"); });\n}\n\nfunction ppgSampleFrame() {\n  if (!ppgSampling) { return; }\n  var video = document.getElementById(\"ppg-video\");\n  if (video.videoWidth > 0) {\n    // Центральная область кадра — средний зелёный канал (самый\n    // пульсативный). Кадр умирает в canvas: ни копий, ни передачи.\n    ppgCtx.drawImage(video, 8, 8, 16, 16, 0, 0, 8, 8);\n    var d = ppgCtx.getImageData(0, 0, 8, 8).data;\n    var sum = 0;\n    for (var i = 0; i < d.length; i += 4) { sum += d[i + 1]; }\n    ppgSamples.push({ t: performance.now() - ppgStart_, v: sum / (d.length / 4) });\n  }\n  var el = Math.round((performance.now() - ppgStart_) / 1000);\n  document.getElementById(\"ppg-timer\").textContent = \"Запись: \" + el + \" с (отсчётов \" + ppgSamples.length + \")\";\n  requestAnimationFrame(ppgSampleFrame);\n}\n\nfunction ppgStop() {\n  if (!ppgSampling) { return; }\n  ppgSampling = false;\n  if (ppgStream) {\n    var tracks = ppgStream.getTracks();\n    for (var i = 0; i < tracks.length; i++) { tracks[i].stop(); }\n    ppgStream = null;\n  }\n  document.getElementById(\"ppg-start-btn\").disabled = false;\n  document.getElementById(\"ppg-stop-btn\").disabled = true;\n  var ex = ppgExtractRR(ppgSamples);\n  var refusal = ppgQualityRefusal(ex);\n  if (refusal !== \"\") {\n    status(refusal + \" — запись НЕ сохранена, повторите с хорошим сигналом\", \"err\");\n    document.getElementById(\"ppg-summary\").textContent = \"Эпох: \" + ex.epochsTotal + \", отбраковано: \" + ex.epochsRejected;\n    return;\n  }\n  rrBuffer = ex.rr;\n  var mean = ex.rr.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + b; }, 0) / ex.rr.length;\n  document.getElementById(\"ppg-save-btn\").disabled = false;\n  document.getElementById(\"ppg-summary\").textContent =\n    \"RR: \" + ex.rr.length + \" · средний \" + Math.round(mean) + \" мс (\" + Math.round(60000 / mean) + \" уд/мин) · эпохи: \" +\n    (ex.epochsTotal - ex.epochsRejected) + \"/\" + ex.epochsTotal + \" годных\";\n  status(\"Сигнал годен — сохраните в сессию или перепишите\", \"ok\");\n}\n\nfunction ppgSave() {\n  if (!sessionId) { status(\"Сначала начните сессию (это отдельная сессия PPG)\", \"err\"); return; }\n  if (!rrBuffer.length) { status(\"RR-ряда нет — сначала запишите сигнал\", \"err\"); return; }\n  api(\"/miniapp/session/close\", {\n    id: String(sessionId),\n    steps_done: String(marks.length),\n    step_marks: JSON.stringify(marks),\n    rr_json: JSON.stringify(rrBuffer),\n    rr_source: \"ppg\"\n  })\n    .then(function (res) {\n      if (res.code === 403 && res.body.indexOf(\"CSRF\") >= 0) { location.reload(); return; }\n      if (res.code !== 200) { status(\"Отказ сервера: \" + res.code + \" \" + res.body, \"err\"); return; }\n      status(\"RR-ряд (\" + rrBuffer.length + \" интервалов) записан в сессию \" + sessionId, \"ok\");\n    })\n    .catch(function (e) { status(\"Ошибка сети: \" + e, \"err\"); });\n}\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}

// Open a practice session (the Н2-03 skeleton writer; the Н2-04/Н2-05
// screens are its clients). BOUNDARY pattern (the process_updates
// precedent of Н1-06): the route validates shapes loudly (whitelists,
// numeric guards over the escape bridge) and passes the values; inside
// the annotated parameters the data is sanctioned and the writers run.
// arm_id/trial_id below 1 mean "no linkage" and land as SQL NULL (the
// CASE form keeps ONE parameterized statement; 0 is never stored, so
// the FK clauses stay truthful under the enforced-references replay).
// Returns the new row id.
pattern miniapp_session_open(kind: String<public, trusted>, tempo_bpm: Float, steps_total: Float,
                             session_date: String<public, trusted>, arm_id: Float, trial_id: Float) -> Float {
  let _ = db_execute("INSERT INTO practice_session (kind, tempo_bpm, steps_total, session_date, arm_id, trial_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, CASE WHEN ? > 0 THEN ? END, CASE WHEN ? > 0 THEN ? END)", [kind, tempo_bpm, steps_total, session_date, arm_id, arm_id, trial_id, trial_id])
  let rows = query("SELECT last_insert_rowid() AS id", [])
  return rows[0].id
}

// Close/update a session: the completed-step count, the per-step marks
// and (from Н2-05) the RR series. BOUNDARY pattern: the raw JSON
// strings arrive trusted-by-annotation (the route capped their size
// and the parameterized UPDATE carries them verbatim — SQL-injection
// impossible); the JSON shape is validated by parse_json at every
// READ (garbage never decodes silently). Returns the number of
// updated rows (0 = unknown id — the route answers 404 loudly).
pattern miniapp_session_close(sid: Float, steps_done: Float, step_marks: String<public, trusted>,
                              rr_json: String<public, trusted>, rr_source: String<public, trusted>) -> Float {
  let _ = db_execute("UPDATE practice_session SET steps_done = ?, step_marks = ?, rr_json = ?, rr_source = ? WHERE id = ?", [steps_done, step_marks, rr_json, rr_source, sid])
  let rows = query("SELECT changes() AS n", [])
  return rows[0].n
}

// Read one session back (the module tests + the read path of
// Н2-06/Н2-07; a third-party sqlite3 client reads the same rows —
// invariant 6).
pattern miniapp_session_get(sid: Float) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id, kind, arm_id, trial_id, tempo_bpm, steps_total, steps_done, step_marks, rr_json, rr_source, session_date FROM practice_session WHERE id = ?", [sid])
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: miniapp-core ─────────────────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: telegram-core (byte-identical to
//    src/telegram/telegram.mlog §telegram-core) ────────────────────────

// The OWNER's calendar date of a unix timestamp, "YYYY-MM-DD" (Н2-10):
// pure UTC arithmetic over an explicit offset (hours, local = UTC +
// offset, the same KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET semantics the cron expressions
// use). The system time zone of the process is NEVER consulted —
// date_format_iso is UTC (probe-pinned under TZ=UTC/Moscow/New_York) —
// so the trial date, the tick and the cron schedule share ONE clock.
pattern owner_date(unix_ts: Float, tz_offset_hours: Float) -> String {
  return substring(date_format_iso(unix_ts + tz_offset_hours * 3600.0), 0, 10)
}

// The acceptance-window date: the window of the trial of day D lasts
// until 02:00 of D+1 (the evening tick), so the window date is the
// owner's date of (moment - 2 h). 01:00 D+1 belongs to D; 03:30 D+1
// belongs to D+1, whose trial may not exist yet.
pattern window_date(unix_ts: Float, tz_offset_hours: Float) -> String {
  return owner_date(unix_ts - 7200.0, tz_offset_hours)
}

// Fold local wall-clock minutes to the UTC cron expression for a fixed
// local time. local_minutes = hour*60+minute in the OWNER's wall
// clock, tz_offset_hours = local = UTC + offset. No modulo operator:
// the +2880 pad keeps the subtraction non-negative before the
// truncating division (the bandit explore-idx precedent).
pattern cron_expr_for(local_minutes: Float, tz_offset_hours: Float) -> String {
  let off_min = to_int(tz_offset_hours * 60.0)
  let shifted = local_minutes - to_float(off_min) + 2880.0
  let day = to_int(shifted / 1440.0)
  let modm = shifted - day * 1440.0
  let hh = to_int(modm / 60.0)
  let mm = modm - hh * 60.0
  return to_string(mm) + " " + to_string(hh) + " * * *"
}

// Н2-13: the weekly report DAY guard. The cron store accepts only
// 5-field expressions (probe-pinned: a dow field answers
// [CRON_JOB_FAILED] expects a 5-field expression), so the weekly job
// is registered DAILY at 09:30 local and the tick self-guards on the
// local weekday: date_parts.weekday is 0-based from Monday
// (probe-pinned: 2026-10-23, a Friday, carries weekday=4) — Monday = 0.
// A daily fire that sends once a week; the alternative does not exist
// in the cron subsystem (declared loudly).
pattern is_weekly_report_day(now_ts: Float) -> Bool {
  let p = date_parts(now_ts)
  return p.weekday == 0.0
}

// Parse one chat text into the protocol answer. Returns
// {kind: "prediction"|"moment"|"note", value: Float, text: String}.
// to_float fails LOUD on garbage (the m0_row precedent) — a malformed
// p:/m: answer degrades to a note, never to a silent zero.
pattern parse_chat_text(raw_text: String) -> Struct {
  let text = trim(raw_text)
  if starts_with(text, "p:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 2, len(text)))
    // №514: to_float fails LOUD on garbage — a malformed answer
    // degrades to a note through the explicit -1 sentinel, never to a
    // silent zero (a silent zero would fabricate a prediction).
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "prediction", value: v, text: text}
  }
  if starts_with(text, "m:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 2, len(text)))
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "moment", value: v, text: text}
  }
  // Н2-12: the full-reward protocol — «сдвиг через сутки» (nd:) и
  // «действие в сторону ноты за 72 часа» (act:). The same -1 sentinel:
  // garbage degrades to a note, never to a fabricated component value.
  if starts_with(text, "nd:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 3, len(text)))
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "next_day", value: v, text: text}
  }
  if starts_with(text, "act:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 4, len(text)))
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "action", value: v, text: text}
  }
  // Н2-13: the optional sleep context (s:0..1) — the ONLY source of
  // sleep_quality in the Telegram circuit; when it is absent the value
  // is NOT fabricated (the silent zero is forbidden — the -1 sentinel
  // stands for «не отвечено», declared in the PR).
  if starts_with(text, "s:") {
    let rest = trim(substring(text, 2, len(text)))
    let v = to_float_or(rest, 0 - 1.0)
    if v < 0.0 {
      return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
    }
    return {kind: "sleep", value: v, text: text}
  }
  // Н2-13: the honesty-valve report on request (the proposed word;
  // both the Russian and the latin form map to one kind).
  if starts_with(text, "отчёт") or starts_with(text, "report") {
    return {kind: "report", value: 0.0, text: text}
  }
  return {kind: "note", value: 0.0, text: text}
}

// The morning proposal message. Every dynamic fragment passes
// escape_html — the acceptance row: DB output never reaches the chat
// raw. Н2-09: the practice body is a third fragment — the proposal
// must tell what to do, not just name the hand. Н2-11: the proposal
// names BOTH answer formats — p: now, the m: request arrives in the
// evening collect tick.
pattern format_proposal(arm_name: String, practice_body: String, note_body: String) -> String {
  return "Проба дня: " + escape_html(arm_name) + ".\nПрактика: " + escape_html(practice_body) + "\nНота: " + escape_html(note_body) + "\nОтветь предсказанием: p:0..1. Вечером придёт сбор отклика: m:0..1"
}

// The morning proposal row: arm name + optional note body + the group
// practice text. SQL NULL from the LEFT JOIN materializes as Unit on
// 0.30.0 (probe-pinned, Н2-01) — escape_html would fail-closed
// [TYPE_MISMATCH] inside the first seeded proposal (the body would not
// be a String), so the note is COALESCEd to a String here. Н2-09: the
// practice text joins by arm.group_name; a missing or empty row
// degrades LOUD to «(нет текста практики)» — NULLIF lifts the empty
// string into the same COALESCE fallback, never a silent blank.
pattern morning_proposal_row(tid: Float) -> List {
  return query("SELECT a.name, COALESCE(n.body, '') AS body, COALESCE(NULLIF(p.body, ''), '(нет текста практики)') AS practice FROM trial t JOIN arm a ON a.id = t.arm_id LEFT JOIN note n ON n.id = t.note_id LEFT JOIN practice_text p ON p.group_name = a.group_name WHERE t.id = ?", [tid])
}

// The evening report message.
pattern format_report(processed: Float, closed: Float, predictions: Float, moments: Float) -> String {
  return "Отчёт: обработано " + escape_html(to_string(processed)) + ", закрыто пропуском " + escape_html(to_string(closed)) + ", предсказаний " + escape_html(to_string(predictions)) + ", откликов " + escape_html(to_string(moments))
}

// Н2-11: the evening collect request. ONE message per evening, sent by
// tg_collect_tick ONLY when today's window still holds an open trial
// with no moment (pending_collect_trial below); silence otherwise. No
// reminders: a skip is the normal outcome, never chased (the concept's
// load norm). The text is STATIC — no DB fragment rides in it, so
// escape_html has nothing to lift; the wording is the proposed legend
// (шкала m:), pending the owner's approval per the naryad Шаг 0 —
// replaceable by this one string.
pattern format_collect_request() -> String {
  return "Вечерний сбор: как прошла проба? Один отклик в моменте: m:0..1 — 0 совсем не то состояние, 1 полностью оно. Пропустить можно просто не отвечая: окно закроется в 02:00."
}

// The collect-tick decision (Н2-11): the open trial of the window that
// still lacks the moment — the request fires exactly when this returns
// a row. The moment guard rides the response table (the ANY-moment
// count, the same guard apply_answer and the spectral projection use):
// a moment already given — subjective or spectral — silences the tick.
pattern pending_collect_trial(window_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT t.id FROM trial t WHERE t.status = 'proposed' AND t.trial_date = ? AND t.arm_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM response r WHERE r.trial_id = t.id AND r.kind = 'moment') ORDER BY t.id DESC LIMIT 1", [window_date])
}

// Н2-12: the full-reward question helpers. The asks ride the morning
// tick (D+1 asks «сдвиг» about D's trial, D+3 asks «действие» about
// D's trial — ADR-0001's 72-hour component). Only COMPLETED trials are
// asked about: the moment arrived, the practice is confirmed — asking
// about a silent window would presuppose a practice that never was.
// Unanswered components stay ABSENT (present flag 0, ADR-0001) — the
// silence is never rewritten into a zero.
// Н2-13: the sleep context binds to the window's LATEST trial in ANY
// status — a completed trial (the practice done, the sleep note about
// that day arrives late) must still accept it; a missed one too (the
// row stays blind — the read guard keys on response rows).
pattern latest_window_trial(window_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT id FROM trial WHERE trial_date = ? AND arm_id IS NOT NULL ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1", [window_date])
}

pattern pending_next_day_trial(window_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT t.id FROM trial t WHERE t.status = 'completed' AND t.trial_date = ? AND t.arm_id IS NOT NULL AND t.next_day_present = 0 ORDER BY t.id DESC LIMIT 1", [window_date])
}

pattern pending_action_trial(window_date: String) -> List {
  return query("SELECT t.id FROM trial t WHERE t.status = 'completed' AND t.trial_date = ? AND t.arm_id IS NOT NULL AND t.action_present = 0 ORDER BY t.id DESC LIMIT 1", [window_date])
}

// The question texts (STATIC — proposed wording, pending the owner's
// approval per the naryad Шаг 0; replaceable by these one strings).
pattern format_next_day_question() -> String {
  return "Сдвиг после вчерашней пробы? Один ответ: nd:0..1 (0 — никакого сдвига, 1 — явный)"
}

pattern format_action_question() -> String {
  return "Действие в сторону ноты за 72 часа? Один ответ: act:0..1 (0 — не было, 1 — было и двигает)"
}

// The getUpdates URL with the offset + the long-poll timeout. The
// token lives in the URL path (the Bot API contract); it is read from
// the environment at the call site and never printed or echoed.
pattern get_updates_url(token: String, offset: Float) -> String {
  return "https://api.telegram.org/bot" + token + "/getUpdates?offset=" + to_string(offset) + "&timeout=25"
}

// One long-poll getUpdates with the №592 per-call deadline and the
// three-attempt caller-side retry (the language hides no retry inside,
// CHANGELOG-282). Returns the parsed update LIST — UNTRUSTED network
// data; the consumer must run it through the annotated boundary
// (process_updates). Empty List on exhausted retry: the caller
// distinguishes the drain outcome by the offset, silence is never
// fabricated as data.
// http_get returns the body as a RAW STRING (probe-pinned 2026-10-08):
// parse_json before json_get is mandatory — a direct json_get on the
// String silently returns the default and the drain sees an empty list.
pattern fetch_updates(token: String, offset: Float) -> List {
  let url = get_updates_url(token, offset)
  let mut attempt = 0.0
  while attempt < 3.0 {
    attempt = attempt + 1.0
    let r = try http_get(url, 40.0)
    // mlog 0.34.1: the guard is ct_eq over to_string(r.ok) — constant-time
    // equality is the sanctioned anti-injection decision (№806): the
    // untrusted try outcome never decides a bare if. The same-line
    // allow(unchecked_result) covers the analyzer gap (the guard proof is
    // not carried into the while body; probe-pinned on v0.34.1) — the
    // value is read ONLY when ct_eq admitted the branch (r.ok == "true").
    if ct_eq(to_string(r.ok), "true") {
      return json_get(parse_json(to_string(r.value)), "result", []) // allow(unchecked_result): ct_eq guard admits .value only on r.ok == "true"
    }
    if attempt < 3.0 {
      sleep(15.0)
    }
  }
  return []
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: telegram-core

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: context-core (byte-identical to
//    src/context/context.mlog §context-core) ─────────────────────────
// ── Moon arithmetic (synodic, no external libraries) ──────────────────

entity MOON_EPOCH: Float = 947182440.0
entity SYNODIC: Float = 29.530588853

// Age of the moon in days, [0, SYNODIC). The language has no modulo:
// `x - to_int(x/syn)*syn` is fmod for positive x (truncating to_int),
// identical to the reference implementation's double math.
pattern moon_age(unix: Float) -> Float {
  let diff_days = (unix - MOON_EPOCH) / 86400.0
  let cycles = to_int(diff_days / SYNODIC)
  return diff_days - cycles * SYNODIC
}

// Eight equal sectors of syn/8 starting AT the new moon (age 0):
// new [0, 3.6913), waxing_crescent [3.6913, 7.3826), first_quarter
// [7.3826, 11.0740), waxing_gibbous [11.0740, 14.7653), full
// [14.7653, 18.4566), waning_gibbous [18.4566, 22.1479), last_quarter
// [22.1479, 25.8392), waning_crescent [25.8392, 29.5306).
// age < SYNODIC by construction, so to_int lands in 0..7.
pattern moon_phase_name(age: Float) -> String {
  let sector = to_int(age / (SYNODIC / 8.0))
  if sector < 1 { return "new_moon" }
  if sector < 2 { return "waxing_crescent" }
  if sector < 3 { return "first_quarter" }
  if sector < 4 { return "waxing_gibbous" }
  if sector < 5 { return "full_moon" }
  if sector < 6 { return "waning_gibbous" }
  if sector < 7 { return "last_quarter" }
  if sector < 8 { return "waning_crescent" }
  return "new_moon"
}

// Synodic day 1..30 (age 0.0 -> day 1; age 29.5 -> day 30; the wrap to
// day 1 happens through moon_age at the synodic boundary).
pattern moon_day(age: Float) -> Float {
  return to_int(age) + 1.0
}

// The stored form: BOTH the phase and the synodic day in one
// machine-readable string (the context table has no moon-day column;
// decision 4 above). Pinned by a test.
pattern moon_record(unix: Float) -> String {
  let age = moon_age(unix)
  return "phase=" + moon_phase_name(age) + "|day=" + to_string(moon_day(age))
}

// ── Day window (concept schedule; decision 5) ─────────────────────────

// morning = local 07:00..21:29, evening = 21:30..06:59. Flat guard
// chain — no nested-if returns (the Н1-06 §2 lesson). The UTC instant
// stays UTC; only the display window folds through tz_offset.
pattern day_window_for(unix: Float, tz_offset: Float) -> String {
  let local = unix + tz_offset * 3600.0
  let day_sec = local - to_int(local / 86400.0) * 86400.0
  let hour_frac = day_sec / 3600.0
  if hour_frac < 7.0 { return "evening" }
  if hour_frac < 21.5 { return "morning" }
  return "evening"
}

// ── Blind logging (инвариант 2; decision 1) ───────────────────────────

// Writes the context row ALWAYS (at probe time) and returns the row id.
// weather/sound_mode stay empty in wave 1 (no weather feed, no sound
// modes in the arm space — the M3 reserve); the columns exist in the
// store schema and future providers fill them without a migration.
pattern collect_context(trial_id: Float, now: Float, sleep_quality: Float) -> Float {
  let rec = moon_record(now)
  return db_insert("context", {trial_id: trial_id, moon_phase: rec, weather: "", sound_mode: "", sleep_quality: sleep_quality})
}

// The ONLY read API. Blind (returns "") until a response row exists for
// the trial — decision 1. After the response the full record opens:
// "<moon_phase>|sleep_quality=<v>|weather=<w>|sound_mode=<s>|logged_at=<ts>"
// (moon_phase itself is "phase=…|day=…"). The consumers branch on the
// empty string — the one loud blindness contract.
pattern read_context(trial_id: Float) -> String {
  let resp = query("SELECT count(*) AS n FROM response WHERE trial_id = ?", [trial_id])
  if resp[0].n < 1.0 { return "" }
  let rows = query("SELECT trial_id, moon_phase, weather, sound_mode, sleep_quality, logged_at FROM context WHERE trial_id = ?", [trial_id])
  return rows[0].moon_phase + "|sleep_quality=" + to_string(rows[0].sleep_quality) + "|weather=" + rows[0].weather + "|sound_mode=" + rows[0].sound_mode + "|logged_at=" + rows[0].logged_at
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: context-core ─────────────────────────────────────

// ── APP-MIRROR-START: honesty-report-core (byte-identical to
//    src/report/report.mlog §honesty-report-core) ─────────────────────
// ── The honesty math ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

// The bandit side: every completed trial is a bandit pick with its
// realized reward. The population variance form is declared (decision 2).
// Returns the map {n, m, se} — the reward mean and its SE over the
// completed picks.
pattern bandit_side() -> map {
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS n, avg(reward) AS m, avg(reward * reward) AS m2 FROM trial WHERE status = 'completed'", [])
  let n = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].n), 0.0)
  let m = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].m), 0.0)
  let m2 = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].m2), 0.0)
  let mut var = m2 - m * m
  if var < 0.0 { let var = 0.0 }
  let mut se = 0.0
  if n > 0.0 {
    let se = sqrt(var / n)
  }
  return {n: n, m: m, se: se}
}

// The random-choice baseline: the unweighted mean of the per-arm mean
// rewards (decision 1). Returns the map {arms, m, se} — the arm count
// and the baseline mean with its SE across arm means.
pattern random_baseline() -> map {
  let rows = query("SELECT count(*) AS arms, avg(m) AS m, avg(m * m) AS m2 FROM (SELECT arm_id, avg(reward) AS m FROM trial WHERE status = 'completed' GROUP BY arm_id)", [])
  let k = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].arms), 0.0)
  let m = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].m), 0.0)
  let m2 = to_float_or(to_string(rows[0].m2), 0.0)
  let mut var = m2 - m * m
  if var < 0.0 { let var = 0.0 }
  let mut se = 0.0
  if k > 0.0 {
    let se = sqrt(var / k)
  }
  return {arms: k, m: m, se: se}
}

// A number in the report form: rounded to hundredths, no long tails.
pattern fmt2(x: Float) -> String {
  return to_string(round(x * 100.0) / 100.0)
}

// The verdict (decision 3). The band edges mb ∓ 1.96·se_b are compared
// against the baseline constant.
pattern honesty_verdict() -> String {
  let b = bandit_side()
  if b.n < 1.0 { return "сигнала нет — данных нет (completed=0)" }
  let r = random_baseline()
  let lo = b.m - 1.96 * b.se
  let hi = b.m + 1.96 * b.se
  if lo > r.m { return "выигрыш есть — бандит лучше случайного выбора" }
  if hi < r.m { return "выигрыша нет — хуже случайного выбора" }
  return "сигнала нет — выигрыш над случайным выбором не выявлен"
}

// The gain line: expected [low; high], all three present — no point
// estimate is ever printed alone (the acceptance row).
pattern gain_line() -> String {
  let b = bandit_side()
  let r = random_baseline()
  let lo = b.m - 1.96 * b.se - r.m
  let hi = b.m + 1.96 * b.se - r.m
  return "gain: expected=" + fmt2(b.m - r.m) + " [low=" + fmt2(lo) + "; high=" + fmt2(hi) + "] (95% approx)"
}

// Misses per arm — one aggregate line (decision 4): the fraction of
// missed trials per arm, every arm, SQL-carried order.
pattern misses_line() -> String {
  let rows = query("SELECT group_concat(t.g || ': ' || t.miss || '/' || t.n || ' (' || t.pct || '%)', '; ') AS s FROM (SELECT arm.name AS g, CAST(sum(CASE WHEN trial.status = 'missed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS INT) AS miss, CAST(count(*) AS INT) AS n, CAST(CAST(sum(CASE WHEN trial.status = 'missed' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS REAL) * 100.0 / count(*) AS INT) AS pct FROM trial JOIN arm ON arm.id = trial.arm_id GROUP BY arm.name ORDER BY arm.name) AS t", [])
  if to_string(rows[0].s) == "" { return "misses: (нет проб)" }
  return "misses: " + to_string(rows[0].s)
}

// Moment sources, SEPARATE per source (ADR-0001 — no silent mixing):
// count and mean per source; the default empty source is listed as
// "(пусто)" so a silent default can never hide.
pattern source_lines() -> String {
  let rows = query("SELECT group_concat(CASE WHEN t.src = '' THEN '(пусто)' ELSE t.src END || ': n=' || CAST(t.n AS INT) || ' avg=' || CAST(ROUND(t.m, 2) AS TEXT), '; ') AS s FROM (SELECT moment_source AS src, count(*) AS n, avg(moment_value) AS m FROM trial WHERE moment_present = 1 GROUP BY moment_source ORDER BY moment_source) AS t", [])
  if to_string(rows[0].s) == "" { return "moment sources: (нет момент-откликов)" }
  return "moment sources: " + to_string(rows[0].s)
}

// The SSOT report text. The chat and CLI forms live in
// src/report/report.mlog (the mirror half of this naryad) and are
// derived from THIS text — one source, two presentations.
pattern honesty_report_text() -> String {
  let head = "honesty report\nverdict: " + honesty_verdict()
  let b = bandit_side()
  let r = random_baseline()
  let counts = "\ncompleted=" + to_string(round(b.n)) + " trials over " + to_string(round(r.arms)) + " arms"
  return head + counts + "\n" + gain_line() + "\n" + misses_line() + "\n" + source_lines()
}

// ── The presentation forms ────────────────────────────────────────────

// CLI: print the report to stdout. The assigned-call discipline keeps
// the bare-call defect class (D2/№612) away by construction.
pattern honesty_report_cli() -> Float {
  let text = honesty_report_text()
  print(text)
  return 1.0
}

// Chat: the escape_html-wrapped SSOT text — chat-ready, no raw output.
pattern honesty_report_chat() -> String {
  return escape_html(honesty_report_text())
}
// ── APP-MIRROR-END: honesty-report-core ──────────────────────────────
// ── The two cron ticks (the naryad: "два cron-тика в одном .mlog") ────

// The morning tick: propose an arm through the bandit core, write the
// trial (status 'proposed', the prediction fields stay at their
// defaults until the owner answers), message the owner. The proposal
// IS the prediction request — the owner answers p: during the day.
// Repeated ticks are safe (Н2-08): the proposal is one per day, a
// repeated tick re-shows the existing trial.
pattern tg_morning_tick() -> Unit {
  // Idempotent schema first: the tables exist even before the token
  // guard fires (the loud refusal must not leave an empty database).
  ensure_schema()
  // The wave-1 arm library seeded idempotently (Н2-01): the loud zero
  // ("Библиотека пуста") was the missing Н1-04 integration into the
  // serve composition — the seed lives in the arms-seed mirror above;
  // UNIQUE(name) + INSERT OR IGNORE make a repeated run a no-op.
  let _ = seed_arms()
  // No early-return under a nested if (the D2-family case 4): the
  // guard inverts into a positive branch that carries the whole tick.
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    let off = to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))
    let today = owner_date(now_unix(), off)
    let tid = bandit_propose(today, now_unix())
    let mut msg = "Библиотека пуста — предложение не сформировано (громкий ноль бандита)"
    if tid != 0.0 {
      let arm_rows = morning_proposal_row(tid)
      if len(arm_rows) > 0.0 {
        msg = format_proposal(arm_rows[0].name, arm_rows[0].practice, arm_rows[0].body)
      } else {
        msg = "Проба дня (trial #" + to_string(tid) + ")"
      }
    }
    // Н2-12: the full-reward asks ride the morning message — the D+1
    // «сдвиг» about yesterday's COMPLETED trial and the D+3 «действие»
    // about the trial of three days ago. Each ask pins its trial into
    // the kv pending (the answer binds by the pending — one trial per
    // question kind, never ambiguous); a successful write clears it.
    // Only completed trials are asked about (the moment confirmed the
    // practice); an unanswered component stays absent, never a zero.
    let yesterday = owner_date(now_unix() - 86400.0, off)
    let nd = pending_next_day_trial(yesterday)
    if len(nd) > 0.0 {
      let _ = kv_set("nd_pending_trial", to_string(nd[0].id))
      msg = msg + "\n" + format_next_day_question()
      print("[telegram] morning tick asks next_day about trial " + to_string(nd[0].id))
    }
    let three_ago = owner_date(now_unix() - 259200.0, off)
    let act = pending_action_trial(three_ago)
    if len(act) > 0.0 {
      let _ = kv_set("act_pending_trial", to_string(act[0].id))
      msg = msg + "\n" + format_action_question()
      print("[telegram] morning tick asks action about trial " + to_string(act[0].id))
    }
    let _ = send_message(chat_id, msg)
    print("[telegram] morning tick proposed trial " + to_string(tid))
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — morning tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// The evening tick: drain getUpdates through the boundary, close the
// unanswered as misses (inside process_updates), report. Runs at 02:00
// LOCAL — the acceptance window closes without manual intervention; the
// message-date binding (Н2-10) routes every answer into its own window
// and the close threshold ends the window of now. The counters report
// stays THIS tick's signature: the collect tick (Н2-11) drains silently.
pattern tg_evening_tick() -> Unit {
  ensure_schema()
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    let offset = to_float_or(kv_get("tg_offset"), 0.0)
    let updates = fetch_updates(token, offset)
    process_updates(updates, chat_id, now_unix(), to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0")), offset, true)
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — evening tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// The evening collect tick (Н2-11): the concept's «сбор отклика 21:30».
// Drains getUpdates FIRST through the same boundary (the answers that
// arrived before 21:30 land in their own windows — the same offset code
// as the 02:00 tick), THEN asks for the moment exactly once: only when
// today's window still holds an open trial without a moment. If the
// moment is already given (subjective or spectral) or there is no
// trial — silence. No reminders, no catch-up: a skip is the normal
// outcome (the load norm), a repeated tick re-checks, never re-asks
// about an answered trial (the pending query guards).
pattern tg_collect_tick() -> Unit {
  ensure_schema()
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    let off = to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))
    let offset = to_float_or(kv_get("tg_offset"), 0.0)
    let updates = fetch_updates(token, offset)
    process_updates(updates, chat_id, now_unix(), off, offset, false)
    let window = window_date(now_unix(), off)
    let pending = pending_collect_trial(window)
    if len(pending) > 0.0 {
      let _ = send_message(chat_id, format_collect_request())
      print("[telegram] collect tick: moment requested for trial " + to_string(pending[0].id))
    }
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — collect tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// The weekly honesty-valve report (Н2-13): once a week, Monday
// morning local — verdict, the gain range, the miss fractions per arm,
// the moment sources separately. Read-only: no drain, no trial writes;
// the text is the escape_html-wrapped SSOT report (the chat form).
// The proposed frequency (the naryad Шаг 0): a daily verdict provokes
// peeking; the weekly one does not.
pattern tg_weekly_tick() -> Unit {
  ensure_schema()
  let token = env_or("KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN", "")
  let chat_id = env_or("KAMERTON_CHAT_ID", "")
  if token != "" and chat_id != "" {
    // The daily fire, the weekly send: the guard is the local Monday
    // (is_weekly_report_day); other days the fire is a silent no-op.
    if is_weekly_report_day(now_unix()) == true {
      let _ = send_message(chat_id, honesty_report_chat())
      print("[telegram] weekly tick: honesty report sent")
    }
  }
  if token == "" or chat_id == "" {
    print("[telegram] KAMERTON_TG_TOKEN/KAMERTON_CHAT_ID not set — weekly tick refuses loudly")
  }
}

// ── The idempotent registration + the serve surface ───────────────────


// Register the two ticks from the allowlisted offset. Idempotent across
// restarts AND repeated calls, AND a TZ-offset change: stale jobs (same
// prompt, a different expr — e.g. after KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET moved) are
// removed loudly, the current pair is added when missing.

mlogserver {
  port: 8461
  middleware: [rate_limit, security_headers, csrf]
  route "/health" method=GET {
    return respond("200 ok")
  }
  // Register the two cron ticks; call once after deploy (curl
  // http://127.0.0.1:8461/setup) — repeated calls and restarts are safe.
  route "/setup" method=GET {
    ensure_schema()
    setup_register()
    return respond(redact("200 jobs=" + escape_html(to_string(len(cron_list()))), "secrets"))  // №706: the count derives from private rows — mlog 0.34.1: respond is a №316 sink, the redact bridge sheds the label (probe-pinned)
  }
  route "/jobs" method=GET {
    let jobs = cron_list()
    let mut lines = ""
    each j in jobs {
      lines = lines + escape_html(j.cron_expr) + " -> " + escape_html(j.prompt) + "\n"
    }
    return respond("200 " + lines)
  }
  // Manual fire for the end-to-end check on a test chat (acceptance).
  // Safe to repeat on a live day (Н2-08): the proposal is one per day,
  // a repeated fire re-shows today's trial instead of a second one.
  route "/fire" method=GET {
    let jobs = cron_list()
    each j in jobs {
      // №706: the id flows private (whole-struct posture) — redact bridge.
      let _ = cron_run(redact(j.id, "secrets"))
    }
    return respond("200 fired")
  }

  // Н2-13: the honesty-valve report on request (localhost/tailnet —
  // the same trust posture as /setup /jobs /fire; the text is the
  // escape_html-wrapped SSOT report — the chat form is chat-ready).
  route "/report" method=GET {
    ensure_schema()
    return respond("200 " + honesty_report_chat())
  }
  // ── Mini App (Н2-03): the page and the practice-session journal ──────
  // ADR-0002 variant (а), private tunnel: the page reaches the phone
  // inside the owner's network. Authorization: the allowlisted
  // KAMERTON_MINIAPP_TOKEN against the ?t= param — the SANITIZED
  // projection decides (escape_html bridge; the deploy token charset
  // is alphanumeric, the bridge is exact for it). A request without or
  // with a wrong token is answered 403 LOUDLY and nothing else runs.
  // Request BODIES are deliberately not consumed: on 0.30.0 the body
  // parsers (json_body/form_data/request_body) return an EMPTY struct
  // (probe n203-json4, declared loudly per §2 in the naryad worklog —
  // задание агенту Metalogos-), so the session API takes its fields
  // through the percent-decoded query params (query_param, №257
  // semantics, probe-green) and answers plain text.
  // CSRF: the mutating routes carry the csrf middleware (double-submit,
  // №262 — the audit gate is blocking; probe n203-csrf pins the dance:
  // GET issues _mlog_csrf, every POST echoes it in X-CSRF-Token, TTL
  // 15 min). The page JS performs it (self-host/miniapp/index.html).
  // Two independent gates stack: the ?t= owner token AND the CSRF
  // token — a wrong value of either answers 403 loudly.
  route "/miniapp" method=GET {
    let stored = env_or("KAMERTON_MINIAPP_TOKEN", "")
    let provided = escape_html(query_param("t"))
    if miniapp_check_token(stored, provided) == false {
      return respond_html_status("403 Forbidden", "Kamerton: доступ только по токену владельца")
    }
    return respond_html(miniapp_html())
  }
  route "/miniapp/session" method=POST {
    let stored = env_or("KAMERTON_MINIAPP_TOKEN", "")
    let provided = escape_html(query_param("t"))
    if miniapp_check_token(stored, provided) == false {
      return respond_html_status("403 Forbidden", "Kamerton: доступ только по токену владельца")
    }
    // Idempotent schema first: the session API is self-sufficient
    // before the first tick (the /setup contract stays undisturbed).
    ensure_schema()
    let kind = escape_html(query_param("kind"))
    if kind != "pacer" and kind != "ppg" and kind != "sweep" {
      return respond_html_status("400 Bad Request", "kind: ожидается pacer, ppg или sweep")
    }
    // The numeric guards ride the escape bridge (sanitize-then-decide:
    // escape_html is exact on digits/dots; garbage keeps failing the
    // guard loudly) — the probe n203-bridge pins the shape.
    let tempo = to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("tempo_bpm")), -1.0)
    let steps = to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("steps_total")), -1.0)
    if tempo < 0.0 or steps < 0.0 {
      return respond_html_status("400 Bad Request", "tempo_bpm/steps_total: ожидается число не меньше 0")
    }
    let sid = miniapp_session_open(kind, tempo, steps, owner_date(now_unix(), to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))), to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("arm_id")), 0.0), to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("trial_id")), 0.0))
    return respond("200 {\"id\":" + escape_html(to_string(sid)) + "}")
  }
  route "/miniapp/session/close" method=POST {
    let stored = env_or("KAMERTON_MINIAPP_TOKEN", "")
    let provided = escape_html(query_param("t"))
    if miniapp_check_token(stored, provided) == false {
      return respond_html_status("403 Forbidden", "Kamerton: доступ только по токену владельца")
    }
    ensure_schema()
    let sid = to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("id")), 0.0)
    if sid < 1.0 {
      return respond_html_status("400 Bad Request", "id: ожидается номер сессии")
    }
    let marks = query_param("step_marks")
    let rr = query_param("rr_json")
    // The cap rides the escaped copies: escape only GROWS a string, so
    // the limit is conservative against the raw input.
    if len(escape_html(marks)) > 32768.0 or len(escape_html(rr)) > 32768.0 {
      return respond_html_status("400 Bad Request", "поле превышает 32KiB")
    }
    let source = escape_html(query_param("rr_source"))
    if source != "ppg" and source != "manual" and source != "" {
      return respond_html_status("400 Bad Request", "rr_source: ожидается ppg, manual или пусто")
    }
    let updated = miniapp_session_close(sid, to_float_or(escape_html(query_param("steps_done")), 0.0), marks, rr, source)
    // The rowcount comes from the DB lane (untrusted by the store
    // discipline); the decision rides the SANITIZED projection — the
    // fetch_updates precedent (escape_html decides, the raw never does).
    // Return-type annotations are outside the grammar (probe
    // n203-retann, parse error) — declared loudly in the naryad worklog.
    if to_float_or(escape_html(to_string(updated)), 0.0) < 1.0 {
      return respond_html_status("404 Not Found", "сессия не найдена")
    }
    // Н2-06: the sweep verdict rides the FINAL close of a sweep session
    // (final=1 — the page sends it from «Завершить» only; the per-step
    // incremental closes never trigger the analysis). The verdict is
    // computed from the session's own step_marks: the per-step spectra
    // (№591 builtins), the max-share pick, the prereg gate (>= 6 valid
    // steps), the sweep_result row + the kv mirror. A refused protocol
    // answers 200 with ok=false and the loud reason — the close itself
    // succeeded; no row, no kv write on refusal.
    let final = escape_html(query_param("final"))
    if final == "1" {
      let rows = miniapp_session_get(sid)
      if len(rows) > 0.0 {
        if rows[0].kind == "sweep" {
          let res = sweep_analyze(rows[0].step_marks)
          if res.ok == true {
            let rec = sweep_record(sid, res, owner_date(now_unix(), to_float(env_or("KAMERTON_TZ_OFFSET", "0"))))
            // Н2-07: the accepted run fixes the LINKED trial's moment by
            // the spectral source — the winner's power fraction is the
            // honest resonance measure (ADR-0001 priority).
            let mut mom = ""
            if type_of(rows[0].trial_id) == "Float" {
              if rows[0].trial_id > 0.0 {
                let mw = moment_spectral_write(rows[0].trial_id, rec.share, rec.peak_freq_bpm / 60.0)
                if mw > 0.0 {
                  mom = ",\"moment\":{\"written\":1,\"share\":" + to_string(rec.share) + ",\"peak_hz\":" + to_string(rec.peak_freq_bpm / 60.0) + "}"
                }
              }
            }
            return respond("200 {\"updated\":" + escape_html(to_string(updated)) + ",\"sweep\":" + json_encode(rec) + mom + "}")
          }
          return respond("200 {\"updated\":" + escape_html(to_string(updated)) + ",\"sweep\":" + json_encode(res) + "}")
        }
        if rows[0].kind == "ppg" {
          // Н2-07: the linked ppg session's RR series -> the spectral
          // moment; a refusing series stays loud and the subjective
          // fallback remains untouched (no fabricated value).
          let mut mom = ""
          if type_of(rows[0].trial_id) == "Float" {
            if rows[0].trial_id > 0.0 {
              if rows[0].rr_json != "" {
                let rr = parse_json(rows[0].rr_json)
                if type_of(rr) == "List" {
                  let mv = moment_spectral_from_rr(rr)
                  if mv.ok == true {
                    let mw = moment_spectral_write(rows[0].trial_id, mv.share, mv.peak_hz)
                    if mw > 0.0 {
                      mom = ",\"moment\":{\"written\":1,\"share\":" + to_string(mv.share) + ",\"peak_hz\":" + to_string(mv.peak_hz) + "}"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
          return respond("200 {\"updated\":" + escape_html(to_string(updated)) + mom + "}")
        }
      }
    }
    return respond("200 {\"updated\":" + escape_html(to_string(updated)) + "}")
  }
}

// ── Tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The suite is network-free: send_message degrades to the [AUDIT] stub
// without TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (probe-pinned), fetch_updates is exercised
// against a refused endpoint through its retry/backoff shape, the DB
// effects run on the in-memory store.








